      "name": "9/11 Memorial & Museum Admission + Statue of Liberty Guided Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>HighlightsVisit the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island with a knowledgeable guideSkip the lines with priority boarding for the ferry across New York HarborDiscover moving immigrant stories at the Ellis Island Immigration MuseumHear moving stories about the tragic events of 2001 at the 9/11 MuseumReflect at the 9/11 Memorial Pools honoring those who diedExplore the of New York’s most iconic landmarks with a guided tour of the Statue of Liberty &amp; Ellis Island, followed by a flexible entry ticket to the 9/11 Memorial &amp; Museum. Choose a guide in English, Spanish, or French and skip the lines with pre-reserved tickets.Start your journey at Battery Park, where your guide sets the scene before you board the ferry to Liberty Island. Enjoy stunning views of the New York Harbor and Manhattan skyline as you sail.On Liberty Island, uncover the history of Lady Liberty, designed by Gustave Eiffel, and her powerful symbolism. Snap photos from the best spots and enjoy some free time to explore the “Statue of Liberty Museum” before heading to Ellis Island.At Ellis Island, discover the immigrant experience with your guide, exploring how millions began their new lives in America. Visit the Immigration Museum and hear moving stories of hope and resilience before hearing back to Battery Park on the Ferry.Then make your way to the nearby 9/11 Memorial and Museum, where your flexible entry ticket will give you access to the Museum. Reflect on the events of September 11, 2001 at this award-winning museum featuring artifacts &amp; exhibits linked to the events of 9/11.Visit the National September 9/11 memorial located next door featuring twin reflecting polls which sit within the footprints where the Twin Towers once stood.</p></div>",
