      "name": "Harlem Gospel and Brunch Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>This tour will lead you through Mount Morris Park Historical District area. Here you will find a multitude of churches rich with history where America's founding fathers made their homes. Some of the most well known musicians and entertainers started their journeys there too.\n\nHeading through uptown on a Sunday morning you will hear and enjoy the sights and sounds of Harlem at its best. What is more, you will be able to participate in sermons and homilies given by Harlem's most prominent. Celebrate with the world famous congregational choirs of the Convent Avenue Baptist Church, United House of Prayer, Abyssinian Baptist Church and the Roman Catholic Church of the Resurrection, whose renowned singers will have you jumping in your seat.\n\nAfterwards, you can top off the day with some of the area's best kept secrets- fine dining at reasonable prices. Allow Harlem's finest culinary masters delight and tempt you with their authentic ethnic delights - just for you!</p></div>",
