      "name": "Big Apple in Lights Private Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>duration: 4 - 6 Hours\n\ncancellation_summary: Free Cancellation up to 48 Hours in Advance\n\nmeeting_point: 770 7th Ave, New York, NY 10019\n\nmax_age: 99\n\ngroup_size: 15\n\ndescription: Experience awesome New York City sites at night, as you hop aboard our unique glass-top convertible bus for a comprehensive, private bus tour of NYC at night!\nYour tour guide will accompany you and will get off with you at each stop, helping you discover a different side of New York City!\nThe tour typically starts in the Times Square area, on 7th Avenue between 50th and 51st Streets, but you’re welcome to choose a different location in Manhattan as your designated pick-up and drop-off point.\nWe leave our starting/ending location in Times Square and head to our first stop – one of the most fascinating attractions in New York City – the High Line Park. The stop features a 15-minute walk along the elevated, linear park, which was originally a railway dating back to the industrial days of the west side of Manhattan.\nWe continue our guided walk to NYC’s newest outdoor space – Little Island – a 2.4-acre public park on the Hudson River.\nOff to Pier 17 at the historic South Street Seaport for magnificent views of the Downtown Brooklyn skyline and the iconic Brooklyn Bridge at night!\nWe make a stop in Lower Manhattan for a quick bite at a local pizza spot downtown, where you’ll also have access to other nearby local food spots. Please note that food and drinks are optional and are not included in the price of your tour ticket.\nOur next stop is Grand Central Terminal for a quick indoor tour of this iconic New York City landmark offering views of the Chrysler Building and NYC’s newest skyscraper – One Vanderbilt!\nThe bus heads back to the heart of NYC – Times Square, our original starting point.\nAdditional sites and neighborhoods you’ll see from the comfort of your bus include the Tribeca neighborhood, where celebrities Robert De Niro and Taylor Swift live, Midtown, Chelsea, East Village, the Financial District, the Meatpacking District, the three bridges along the East River – Brooklyn Bridge, Williamsburg Bridge, and Manhattan Bridge, the Empire State Building, Rockefeller Center, the United Nations Building, One World Trade Center, the MetLife Building, the Chrysler Building, and more!\nYour tour guide will accompany you and will get off the bus with you at each stop, introducing you to a different side of New York City! Join us for a memorable sightseeing experience of NYC at night!\n\nwhat_is_included: + New York City private sightseeing tour by luxury tour vehicle\n\n+ Expert tour guides and live narration\n\n+ Pickup and drop-off\n\n+ Bottled water on buses\n\n+ Guided walks\n\nwhat_is_not_included: – Lunch\n\n– Gratuities\n\nitinerary: + Times Square (Start/End)\n\n+ Hudson Yards and the Highline Park\n\n+ Pier 17 at South Street Seaport\n\n+ Lower Manhattan\n\n+ Grand Central Terminal\n\nhighlights: + Fully guided walks with live narration from friendly and knowledgeable local guides\n\n+ Spectacular views of iconic NYC landmarks\n\n+ Luxury climate-controlled buses for an enjoyable all-weather experience\n\nwhat_to_bring: Comfortable shoes and clothes.\n\ndisclaimers: Our small-capacity tour buses can accommodate foldable wheelchairs and foldable baby strollers, however, if you or a member of your party uses a full-size wheelchair that requires a ramp, we kindly ask you to contact us directly. We're more than happy to make arrangements to accommodate your mobility needs.\nOperational Dates: 7 days a week, rain or shine\nBlackout Days: 4th of July (no night tour), Thanksgiving Day (no night tour), NYC Half-Day Marathon - March (no tours), Christmas Day (no tours) &amp; New Year's Eve (no tours)</p></div>",
