      "name": "NYC Holiday Walking Tour 5th Ave, Rockefeller Tree & Xmas Village",
      "description": "<div><p>HighlightsDiscover the story behind the Rockefeller Christmas TreeAdmire the artistry of the best Holiday Window’s in New YorkExplore the Winter Village in New York with its vast array of food and giftsLet your expert local guide show you New York at its most festiveSee famous landmarks like St Patrick's Cathedral &amp; the Plaza HotelExplore the best of 5th Avenue with an expert local tour guide who will help you discover why New York during the Holiday Season is one of the most magical places on earth.See the gorgeously decorated Christmas windows at luxury department stores like Bergdorf Goodman &amp; Saks, as well as flagship stores like Cartier, Tiffany and more.Discover the stories behind New York’s most famous Christmas Tree at the Rockefeller Center, as well as the legendary ice rink and the Channel Gardens with their rows of Angels.See other sites along the way such as the Plaza Hotel (featured in “Home Alone 2”), St Patrick's Cathedral (New York’s Parish Church) decked out for the holidays and Radio City Music Hall (home to the world famous Rockettes and the Christmas Spectacular Show).After a visit to the New York Library’s famous lions, Patience &amp; Fortitude, adorned with their holiday wreaths, the tour ends up at Bryant Park. Here you will explore the seasonal Winter Village where you can shop and eat, and maybe purchase a ticket to skate on the outdoor skating rink.After this tour post your photos on social media and be the envy of friends all around the world as you share pictures of New York at its most festive.</p></div>",
