      "name": "Ellis Island Statue of Liberty & 911 Memorial Pools Escorted Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>The Ellis Island Statue of Liberty &amp; 911 Memorial Pools Escorted Tour is an informative and emotional experience that combines a visit to two of New York City's most iconic landmarks with a tour of the 9/11 Memorial.The tour begins with a fully escorted walking tour of Ellis Island and Lady Liberty. Your guide will provide a personalized overview of the islands' history and cultural significance, as well as share stories and insights about the millions of immigrants who passed through Ellis Island.After returning to Battery Park by ferry, you will visit the 9/11 Memorial, located next to the newly constructed Freedom Tower. The memorial features two reflecting pools, each nearly an acre in size, where the Twin Towers once stood. The pools are surrounded by bronze parapets engraved with the names of the nearly 3,000 people who lost their lives in the terrorist attacks of September 11, 2001.Your guide will provide informative commentary about the memorial and its significance, sharing stories and insights about the events of 9/11 and the impact they had on New York City and the world.Overall, the Ellis Island Statue of Liberty &amp; 911 Memorial Pools Escorted Tour is a powerful and informative experience that provides visitors with a deeper understanding of the history and significance of these iconic landmarks, as well as the impact of the tragic events of 9/11. With a knowledgeable guide and personalized commentary, you can relax and absorb the sights and sounds of these historic sites.</p></div>",
