      "name": "9/11 Memorial, Statue of Liberty, and Ellis Island Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Are you tired of fighting the crowds at New York's famous landmarks? Join us for an early access tour and beat the rush! Starting at 9:30am, we'll take you on an unforgettable journey through some of the city's most iconic attractions.Our first stop is the 9/11 Memorial, where you'll pay tribute to the lives lost in the tragic events of September 11th, 2001. With early access, you'll have the chance to take in the solemn beauty of the memorial before the crowds arrive, allowing you to reflect and pay your respects in peace.From there, we'll make our way to Wall Street, the financial heart of the city. With early access, you'll have the chance to explore this famous street before it becomes overrun with busy commuters and tourists. Our guide will share fascinating insights and stories about the history of Wall Street, from its origins as a Dutch trading post to its present-day status as the center of global finance. You'll learn about the New York Stock Exchange and other important financial institutions, and see the famous Charging Bull statue, which has become an iconic symbol of Wall Street.Next, we'll head to Battery Park, where you'll take in stunning views of the harbor and the Statue of Liberty. With early access, you'll beat the crowds and have the chance to admire this iconic landmark up close, without having to jostle for position with other tourists. Our guide will share fascinating insights about the history of the statue and the role it has played in shaping the United States and the world.After taking in the beauty of the Statue of Liberty, we'll head to Ellis Island, where you'll learn about the millions of immigrants who passed through this iconic gateway to America. With early access, you'll avoid the long lines and crowds that often plague this popular attraction, giving you more time to explore and learn about this important part of American history.Throughout the tour, our guide will share fascinating stories and insights about the history, culture, and architecture of New York City. You'll gain a deeper appreciation for the city's rich heritage and the role it has played in shaping the United States and the world.So come join us for an unforgettable early access tour of New York's famous landmarks! Our expert guide will show you the best of the city, leaving you with memories that will last a lifetime. And best of all, you'll beat the crowds and enjoy a peaceful and meaningful experience at each of these iconic attractions.</p></div>",
