      "name": "New York - Hop on, Hop Off tour - BB",
      "description": "<div><p>Seeing all the major New York sights is exciting and easy with Big Bus Tours. Simply hop on our red route to Explore Downtown NYC. Every bus features pre-recorded commentary, available in 10 languages.Discover the sights of NYC with Big Bus Tours. Our bus tour routes will introduce you to the city's most famous landmarks and attractions, with pre-recorded commentary given by our expert virtual guides. Explore must-see sights such as the Empire State Building, Times Square, One World Trade Center and more.\n\n\n\nRED - DOWNTOWN ROUTE:\n\nTour Duration: 90 MinutesFrequency: every 15–20 minutesHop-On, Hop-Off New York Day TourSeeing all the major New York sights is exciting and easy with Big  Bus Tours. Simply hop on our red route to Explore Downtown NYC. Every  bus features pre-recorded commentary, available in English and Spanish.\n\nM&amp;M's World7th Ave &amp; W 48th St (Outside M&amp;M World &amp; Majestic Deli)\nFirst bus: 09:30Last bus: 16:30MoMAMadame TussaudsTimes SquareBroadwayRockefeller Center\nTimes Square EastW 42nd St &amp; Broadway (*in front of the Knickerbocker Hotel)\n\nFirst bus: 09:33Last bus: 16:33                                                 \nMadame TussaudsTimes SquareMacy's Department StoreBryant ParkRadiator BuildingBroadwayFifth Avenue\nEmpire State Building / KoreaTown5th Ave &amp; W 32nd St (in front of CVS Pharmacy)\n\nFirst bus: 09:40Last bus: 16:40                                                        \nMacy's Department StoreRadiator BuildingEmpire State Building\nFlatiron District5th Ave &amp; W 23rd St (in front of Eisenbergs Sandwich Shop)\nFirst bus: 09:42Last bus: 16:42\nUnion SquareFlatiron BuildingThe High LineSoHoBroadway and Spring Street (in front of the Nike Store)\nFirst bus: 09:49Last bus: 16:49                                                     ChinatownSoHo\nChinatown / Little Italy100 Lafayette Street (near corner with Walker Street)\nFirst bus:  09:51Last bus:  16:51Chinatown\nBrooklyn BridgePark Row &amp; Beekman St (across from 33 Park Row)\nFirst bus: 09:55Last bus: 16:55\nBrooklyn BridgeWoolworth BuildingOne World Observatory / World Trade CenterTrinity Church9/11 Memorial Museum\nWall Street / Charging BullBroadway &amp; Wall St (Southwest corner near Rector St)\nFirst bus: 10:00Last bus: 17:0040 Wall Street/Trump BuildingWall StreetWoolworth BuildingOne World Observatory / World Trade CenterTrinity Church9/11 Memorial Museum\nStatue of Liberty / Battery ParkState St and Bridge St (in front of the 1 Train Subway Entrance)\nFirst bus: 10:05Last bus: 17:05Statue of LibertyThe Battery40 Wall Street/Trump BuildingWall StreetTrinity Church\nCircle Line Sightseeing12th Ave &amp; 40th St (opposite Pier 81)First bus: 10:20Last bus: 17:20Circle Line Sightseeing CruisesIntrepid Sea, Air and Space Museum\n\n\n\n\nBLUE - UPTOWN ROUTE:\nTour Duration: 75 minutesFrequency: every 60 minutesTimes Square EastW 42nd St &amp; Broadway (*in front of the Knickerbocker Hotel)\nFirst bus: 10:10Last bus: 16:10Madame TussaudsTimes SquareMacy's Department StoreBryant ParkRadiator BuildingBroadwayFifth AvenueTimes Square North7th Ave &amp; W 50th St (in front of Majectic Deli)\nFirst bus: 10:00Last bus: 16:00MoMATimes SquareBroadwayRockefeller Center\nThe Metropolitan Museum of Art5th Ave &amp; E 83rd St (outside the museum near 83rd St)\nFirst bus: 10:45Last bus: 16:45                                               Central ParkGuggenheim MuseumThe Metropolitan Museum of Art\nCentral Park Zoo5th Ave &amp; E 66th St (opposite 845 5th Ave)\nFirst bus: 11:02Last bus: 17:02                                                  The Frick CollectionCentral ParkCentral Park ZooStrawberry Fields\nColumbus CircleCentral Park &amp; Columbus Circle (Southwest corner of Central Park, next to Maine Monument)\nFirst bus: 11:14Last bus: 17:14Columbus CircleCentral ParkCentral Park ZooLincoln CenterStrawberry Fields\n\n\n\n\n</p></div>",
