      "name": "Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island Guided Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>No trip to New York would be complete without visiting and seeing one of the most famous monuments in the world: the Statue of Liberty and the Museum of Immigration on Ellis Island.\nDuration\n4 hours\nAbout\nSince 1886, the Statue of Liberty has hosted millions of people in New York City and the United States. You will get up close and personal with this international symbol, the story behind the statue and how it came to be on Liberty Island.\nTour includes reserved priority access to the islands, a professional New York licensed guide who will escort you through both islands, access to the Statue of Liberty Museum and the Museum National Immigration Office on Ellis Island.\nOn Ellis Island, you will learn about the journey of the millions of immigrants who passed through the island between 1892 and 1924, arriving in the United States in search of a better life.\nDue to site regulations, your guide may not be able to accompany you inside the Museums . However, they will offer a full explanation of what you will experience within.\nOn days where the volume of visitors may be higher, such as: holidays, there may be long lines to enter the ferry, monument and museums.\nFeatured\n• Learn about the history of the Statue of Liberty and the Immigration Museum on Ellis Island\n\n• Stunning views of New York City and the Skyline from Liberty Island\n\n• Learn more about the history of the United States from the 19th to the 21st century.\n\n• Visit the museum of the Statue of Liberty\n\nInclusions\n• Professional licensed guide (if you choose the option)\n\n• Tickets for the ferry to Liberty and Ellis Island \n\n• Entrance to Statue of Liberty Museum\n\n• Entrance to National Museum of Immigration\n\n• Audioguided tour (if you choose the option)\nExclusions\n• Access to the Pedestal and the Crown of Statue of Liberty\n\n• Pick up and drop off from the hotel\n\n• Food and drink\nImportant information\nPlease do not accept directions from people on the street. If you arrive and do not find the place to embark the ferry, or join the guide, you must contact us by replying to this message or via telephone. We cannot be held responsible for information provided by third parties.</p></div>",
