      "name": "9/11 Memorial, Ground Zero & Wall Street Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>HighlightsTour Ground Zero and pause for reflection at the 9/11 Memorial PoolsAdmire the resilience of St Pauls Chapel, Survivor Tree &amp; the local Fire StationDiscover the landmarks of historic Lower Manhattan with a local guideHear stories about Federal Hall, Wall St and the New York Stock ExchangeUpgrade to include skip-the-ticket-line entry to the 9/11 MuseumLet a local guide reveal to you the story of 9/11 as you visit Ground Zero and pay tribute at the 9/11 Memorial Pools to the thousands of citizens and first responders who lost their lives on that fateful day in 2001.Visit St Paul's Chapel, which survived the falling debris of the World Trade Center located 1 block away and was used as a bulletin board to post signs looking for missing family members following the brutal attack.Visit the ground zero fire station where a Memorial Wall visualizes what the first responders faced &amp; did on this day. Learn how events unfolded on that day and how the Memorial Pools were built on the footprint of the Twin Towers. Experience the resilience of the “Survivor Tree”.On this leisurely walking tour you will also explore historic Downtown Manhattan and learn the fascinating stories behind Battery Park, Wall Street, Federal Hall, the New York Stock Exchange and the Financial District. See the site where George Washington was inaugurated as President.Upgrade your tour to include skip-the-ticket-line tickets to the 9/11 Museum which displays over 10,000 artifacts linked to the events of 9/11. The Museum features special exhibits, rotating galleries as well as 3 captivating multi-media permanent exhibitions.</p></div>",
