      "name": "Golden Mile: Fifth Avenue Guided Tour in New York City and optional access to Top of The Rock Observatory",
      "description": "<div><p>Embark on a refined journey through the epitome of sophistication with our exclusive guided tour. In just 2 hours, immerse yourself in the opulent allure of New York City's iconic Fifth Avenue, starting at the illustrious Ritz and culminating in the breathtaking surroundings of Rockefeller Center.\nAbout\nOur exciting Golden Mile tour begins in front of the iconic Ritz Hotel, a symbol of timeless luxury. From here the guide will lead our tour on Fifth Avenue, one of the most prestigious shopping destinations in the world. As we walk down this bustling street, your guide will offer information about the history of fashion in New York and its impact on the city's culture. You'll also learn about the history of the luxury shops and designer boutiques that house this area.\nOur tour will take us to see some of New York's most iconic buildings, such as the famous Trump Tower and the elegant Sherry-Netherland Hotel. You will discover anecdotes about these interesting places and their influence on the city. Other interesting stops will be the Hotel Plaza, Tiffany's Jewelry, the MoMA, or the Apple Store.\nBefore heading to the Rockefeller Center, you will get to know St. Patrick's Cathedral, learning about its stunning architecture, history, and its role as a center of worship in the city also the famous toy store FAO Schwarz, where you will enjoy the magical atmosphere.\nThe last stop is Rockefeller Center, a symbol of New York and home to the famous ice rink and giant Christmas tree during the holidays. The guide will give you all the details about its construction and the symbolism of this building.\nIn case you choose the option, you will finish your experience by climbing to the top of the Top of the Rock observatory to enjoy the best views of New York City.\nGet ready for an unforgettable experience in one of the most fascinating areas of the Big Apple!\nMeeting Point\nOutside the Ritz-Carlton Hotel, 50 Central Park S, New York, NY 10019\nHighlights\n\nStroll Fifth Avenue, one of the most prestigious shopping streets in the world \nPhotograph the emblematic Rockefeller Center, the setting for thousands of films \nPass Trump Tower\nFind some of the most luxurious stores in the Big Apple\nEnjoy the amazing views of New York City from the Top of the Rock observatory if you choose the option \n\nInclusions\n• Professional guide (in English)\n\n• Entrance to Top of the Rock (if you choose the option)\nExclusions\n• Hotel pick up and drop off \n\n• Food and drinks</p></div>",
