      "name": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art: Private 2-hour MET Guided Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>The Metropolitan Museum of Art - known to locals simply as The Met - is one of the world's largest and most famous art museums, with a permanent collection of over two million works of art. With over 5 million visitors each year, there's no better way to experience this legendary institution than with an expert private guide. \n\nOn your <strong>private tour</strong>, you will:\n\nEnjoy a guided tour of the <strong>MET</strong> - the world’s third most-visited art museum;Learn about the <strong>MET'S fascinating history</strong>, the building itself and how the collections were acquired;See renowned paintings by <strong>Botticelli, Da Vinci, Degas, Monet, Picasso, David, Van Gogh, </strong>and more;Explore the extensive collection of sculptures from the <strong>Ancient Greco-Roman</strong> era to <strong>Canova</strong> and <strong>Rodin</strong>; Enjoy the <strong>Egyptian</strong><strong>art</strong> and <strong>architecture</strong> including the ancient <strong>Temple of Dendur</strong>;Enjoy contemporary art including pieces by <strong>Jackson Pollock, Andy Warhol and Jasper Johns;</strong>See the rooms which <strong>starred</strong> in several <strong>iconic</strong><strong>movies</strong> about art theft including <strong>The Thomas Crown Affair and Ocean's Eight</strong>;Learn all about the iconic <strong>MET</strong><strong>Gala</strong> - a major fundraising ball hosted by Vogue each year;Finish your tour inside the museum, where you can continue to explore at your leisure. \nExplore New York's Metropolitan Museum of Art – colloquially referred to as ‘the Met’ with an expert private guide on this fascinating 2-hour tour of the largest museum in the Americas, with one of the most extensive collections of art and historic artefacts in the world: around two million works from over 5000 years of history. \n\nThe Met was founded in the late 19th century by locals who felt the city lacked an adequate art scene. Since then, it has grown to become one of the 50 largest charities in the United States. \n\nOn your private tour, your guide will take you through several museum highlights, including its antiquities collection, which covers everything from the Romans, Egyptians, and Greeks to Polynesia and East Asia. See the Temple of Dendur, recovered from Egypt in the 1960s, and the Sphinx of Hatshepsut, which dates back to the 15th century BC. \n\nThe MET also houses an incredible collection of art from the Renaissance maestros, the Dutch Golden Age, the French Romantics, the Impressionists, and the post-impressionists and more. You will see some of the world’s most famous paintings, and your guide will tell you the life stories of some of the artists - as well as the meanings behind the works of art. \n\nYou'll see truly iconic works by Raphael, Titian, and Caravaggio and Rembrandt's Aristotle with a bust of Homer. The MET also has an enviable collection of Impressionists - including Monet's Waterlilies, Van Gogh's Self Portrait with a Straw Hat, Mary Cassat's 'Young Mother Sewing', and Degas' ballet dancers. There is also a portrait of Gertrude Stein by Picasso - famous for being the wealthy patroness of the so-called 'Lost Generation' in Paris.  \n\nAs well as exquisite sculptures from Ancient Greece and Rome, you will see work by the incomparable Gian Lorenzo Bernini the Italian Baroque genius, exquisite work including Perseus with the Head of Medusa by neo-classical maestro Canova and Rodin's 'Burghers of Calais\". The whole MET experience is truly breathtaking - the architecture of the building as beautiful as the work it houses. \n\nIt is clear why this has become such an iconic place and why it has starred in so many movies over the years - not least films about expensive art heists like the Thomas Crown Affair!\n\nEnd the tour inside to continue at your own leisure. </p></div>",
