      "name": "Niagara Falls One Day Tour from New York City",
      "description": "<div><p>Come join Royal City Tours on a journey to experience the splendor of Niagara Falls, one of the greatest natural wonders of the world - and a must on everyone’s travel bucket list.Each full-day tour offers a unique experience for visitors, whether it is seeing the rainbows dance on the morning mist over the Falls, hearing the resounding roars, or marveling at the magical light show illuminating the night sky. It is a life-changing experience not to be missed!Until you view the majesty of Niagara Falls in person, it is difficult to put into words the unique beauty and unforgettable experience that comes with a trip to see this renowned natural wonder of the world.Our full-day Niagara Falls Tour departs from NYC and will give you a front-row seat to view the resplendent cascading waters of Niagara Falls, up close and in person. We’ll take you on an exciting and breathtaking journey traveling north through the states of New York, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania, culminating in our visit to experience the spectacular beauty of Niagara Falls.The landscape surrounding Niagara Falls is also a sight to behold, so be sure to bring your cameras and your comfiest walking shoes to fully explore Niagara Falls State Park. At over 12,000 years old, Niagara Falls State Park holds the title of the oldest state park in the United States. Our tour guides will provide insider information about the park’s best-hidden gems, and the history of the Falls, and give the best tips for photo opportunities that capture the best angles of the Falls.We’ll also venture out on the legendary Maid of the Mist boat tour, where you’ll experience the larger-than-life Horseshoe Falls from out on the water. In fact, you’ll be so close you’ll feel the misty sprays of the cascading Falls (and may get a little bit wet, so bring a poncho or raincoat!). Out on this unique journey, you’ll see all three of the falls from a jaw-dropping perspective that is simply not possible while on land.On this full-day tour of Niagara Falls, you’ll be given time to wander at your own leisurely pace, take photos, or enjoy some of the area’s best restaurants.Tour PackagesWe offer two Niagara Falls group tour options, each with its own breathtaking charms and unique experiences. A visa is NOT required for either option.11:00 PM DepartureTours that depart from NYC at 11:00 PM (23:00) will have the unique opportunity to experience the Falls in the early morning mist when the rainbows appear to dance off the cascading waters below. When you experience the solitude of the roaring Falls in the early morning hours, it is an experience that will fill your soul with memories to last a lifetime. The tour bus will arrive back in NYC at approximately 10:00 PM (22:00) the following day.7:00 AM DepartureVisitors who choose the 7:00 AM departure will be able to experience the glory of the Falls from day to night, capped off by a multi-colored masterpiece of otherworldly illumination. As the light reflects off the Falls below, this natural wonder of the world will be brought to life with vibrant colors and majestic beauty.Tours that depart at 7:00 AM may also have the opportunity to experience fireworks show you won’t see any other place on earth, with resounding booms, colorful bursts, and glittery sparkles raining down from the night sky directly over the Falls. (Viewing of fireworks is dependent on the seasonal schedule.)Both tour options allow you to experience the unbridled natural beauty of Niagara Falls, a magical place where reality is better than your imagination could have ever dreamed.What Visitors Can Expect From Both Tour Options:· More than 5 hours of time to explore Niagara Falls· “Maid of the Mist” boat ride· Spectacular views of Horseshoe Falls, American Falls, and Bridal Veil Falls· Visits to Goat Island, Luna Island, and all of the Falls’ observatories· NO VISA is required to visit the New York side of the Falls. You may choose to visit the Canadian side on your own if you bring a visa and proper documentation.· This is a bilingual tour and can be performed in both English and Spanish.</p></div>",
