      "name": "NYC: St. Patrick's Cathedral Official Self-Guided Audio Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Highlights● Explore St Patrick's Cathedral at your own pace● Discover the stories behind the stained glass and towering Western Facade● Listen to captivating narration by Cardinal Timothy Dolan and special guests● Enjoy the audio tour in either English, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese or French● There is a special children’s version of the tour which is available in English.Explore St Patrick's Cathedral, the largest gothic-style Catholic cathedral in the United States. Taking up an entire city block, the cathedral opened in 1879. This marble-clad building is considered one of New York City’s finest buildings and is on 5th Ave., opposite the Rockefeller Center.Enjoy expedited entry and a self-guided multi-lingual audio guide. You can listen to the audio tour and explore the Cathedral at your own pace. The audio tour is narrated by Cardinal Timothy Dolan and is about 1 hour long.It is recommended to allow up to 1.5 hours as you may wish to pause the audio tour at times to enjoy features like the Lady Chapel, the towering twin spires, and the 9000 lb. bronze doors which can be opened by a single person.You can also explore the main altar, the stained-glass windows and the Pieta sculpture, 3 times the size of Michelangelo's. The Cathedral has 21 altars and 19 bells, each named after a different saint. Babe Ruth, Andy Warhol and Robert F. Kennedy all had memorial masses here.</p></div>",
