      "name": "Statue of Liberty & Manhattan Skyline Sightseeing Cruise",
      "description": "<div><p>HighlightsSail within 100 feet of the Statue of Liberty and Ellis IslandCruise under the Brooklyn Bridge and pass South Street SeaportMarvel at the skyline of Lower Manhattan from the waterWonder at the Freedom Tower, the tallest building in the Western HemisphereEnjoy English and Spanish commentary highlighting the major landmarksThis 60-minute cruise passes within 100 feet of the Statue of Liberty allowing you to get unbeatable photos of this iconic landmark. Cruise under the Brooklyn Bridge and admire the most famous skyline in the world.Onboard narration will point out the sites as you journey along the river including the Empire State Building, the Freedom Tower, the Manhattan Bridge, Governor's Island, South Street Seaport and more. Use the indoor and outdoor seating and large windows for your viewing pleasure.Pass Ellis Island, where for many years immigrants landed in New York, and then get within touching distance of \"Lady Liberty\" where the boat will pause to allow you to take photos of this famous entry point to New York City.Marvel at the skyline of Manhattan and its famous skyscrapers, including One World Trade Center. Enjoy views of Lower Manhattan from the East River and the famous Hudson River on this roundtrip cruise. Purchase drinks and food from the full bar and concession stand aboard the boat.Upgrade your ticket to include entry to either (or both) of the two main attractions in Lower Manhattan:- One World Observatory, located at the top of the tallest building in the Western hemisphere, with sweeping views of Manhattan and the New York Harbor. Ticket valid anytime for 7 days following your cruise.- 9/11 Museum, the poignant Museum about the attacks of September 11th, 2001, located where the twin towers once stood. Choose your entry time for the Museum and take the cruise at 11am, 12.30pm, 2.30pm, or 4.30pm that same day or the next day.Alternatively, take the 90-minute Night Cruise and see the New York Skyline sparkle in the evening light</p></div>",
