      "name": "Statue of Liberty Cruise and St Patrick's Cathedral Official Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>HighlightsSail within 100 feet of the Statue of Liberty and Ellis IslandCruise under the Brooklyn Bridge with panoramic views of the Manhattan SkylineWonder at the Freedom Tower, the tallest building in the Western HemisphereExplore the largest Gothic-style Catholic Cathedral in the USA at your own paceEnjoy the cathedral audio tour in English, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese or FrenchTake a 60-minute cruise which passes within 100 feet of the Statue of Liberty allowing you to get unbeatable photos of this iconic landmark. Cruise under the Brooklyn Bridge and admire the most famous skyline in the world.With onboard narration in both English &amp; Spanish, marvel at the panoramic views of the Manhattan skyline and its famous landmarks including Ellis Island, the Empire State Building, the Freedom Tower, the Manhattan Bridge, Governor's Island, South Street Seaport and more. Use the indoor and outdoor seating and large windows for your viewing pleasure.Get within touching distance of \"Lady Liberty\" where the boat will pause to allow you to take photos of this famous entry point to New York City.  Purchase drinks and food from the full bar and concession stand aboard the boat.Then head over to St Patrick’s Cathedral and explore its impressive architecture and captivating history on the official self-guided audio tour. You can listen to the audio tour in a choice of 5 languages and explore the Cathedral at your own paceSt Patrick's Cathedral is the largest gothic-style Catholic cathedral in the United States. Taking up an entire city block, the cathedral opened in 1879. This marble-clad building is considered one of New York City’s finest buildings and is on 5th Ave., opposite the Rockefeller Center.</p></div>",
