      "name": "St Patrick's Cathedral Official Holiday Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>HighlightsExplore St Patrick's Cathedral decorated for the Holiday SeasonDiscover the stories behind the stained glass and towering Western FacadeListen to seasonal narration by Cardinal Timothy Dolan and special guestsEnjoy the holiday audio tour in English, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese or FrenchThere is a special children’s version of the tour which is available in English.The most magical time of the year to visit St Patrick’s Cathedral is during the holiday season when the Cathedral is decorated with poinsettias and seasonal displays. It is located on 5th Ave. where the stores feature NYC’s most dazzling holiday window displays, and near the Rockefeller Center, with its enormous Christmas tree and ice-skating rink.The 160-year history of St Patrick’s Cathedral is shared by the men and women who know it best of this special official multilingual holiday audio tour. Enjoy expedited entry and explore the Cathedral at your own pace.St Patrick's Cathedral is the largest gothic-style Catholic cathedral in the United States. Taking up an entire city block, the cathedral opened in 1879. This marble-clad building is considered one of New York City’s finest buildings with its towering twin spires, and the 9000 lb. bronze doors.</p></div>",
