      "name": "Ground Zero and World Trade Center Tour with 911 Museum Upgrade",
      "description": "<div><p>The Ground Zero and World Trade Center Tour with 911 Museum Upgrade is an essential experience for anyone visiting New York City who wants to pay their respects and learn more about the events of September 11, 2001.During the 90-minute tour, you'll visit the grounds of the World Trade Center and see the September 11 Memorial Pool, which serves as a beautiful and poignant tribute to the victims of the attacks. You'll also have the opportunity to hear the personal experiences of your expert local New York City tour guide, who will share their story of that fateful day.The tour concludes at the entrance of the 911 Museum, where you have the option to upgrade to include Priority Skip the Line access to the museum. This upgrade is highly recommended, as the museum is a powerful and emotional experience that offers a deeper understanding of the impact of the attacks on the city and the world.The 911 Museum features a range of exhibits, including artifacts from the Twin Towers, personal stories of survivors and first responders, and multimedia displays that help to bring the events of September 11 to life. The museum is a moving tribute to the victims of the attacks and a testament to the resilience of the city and its people. The Ground Zero and World Trade Center Tour with 911 Museum Upgrade is a must-do experience for anyone visiting New York City who wants to gain a deeper understanding of the events of September 11, 2001, and pay their respects to those who lost their lives in the attacks.</p></div>",
