      "name": "Statue of Liberty Ellis Island plus Double-Decker Bus Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>The Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island are two of the most popular tourist attractions in New York City, and this tour provides a comprehensive and immersive experience of both. The ferry ride to the islands is a highlight of the tour, offering stunning views of the harbor and the Manhattan skyline. This full-day tour is an excellent way to explore two of the most famous landmarks in New York City - the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island. The tour starts and ends at Battery Park, where you have the option to upgrade your experience with a hop-on hop-off double-decker bus tour for one or two days.The tour includes a ferry ride to Liberty Island, where you'll be awestruck by the magnificent Statue of Liberty, a symbol of freedom and democracy. You'll have the opportunity to walk around the island, admire stunning views of the Manhattan skyline, and take photos with Lady Liberty herself. At Liberty Island, you'll be able to climb the pedestal of the Statue of Liberty and enjoy an incredible panoramic view of New York Harbor. You can also visit the Statue of Liberty Museum and learn about the statue's history, construction, and significance as a symbol of freedom.After Liberty Island, the tour takes you to Ellis Island, where you can explore the Immigration Museum and learn about the experiences of millions of immigrants who came to America in search of a better life. You'll be able to see their personal stories, artifacts, and photos, which provide an immersive experience of the history of the United States. On Ellis Island, you can immerse yourself in the history of American immigration and explore the Immigration Museum, which includes exhibits on the arrival process, the experiences of immigrants, and the impact of immigration on the United States. You can even search for your ancestors' records in the American Family Immigration History Center.You can choose to explore the islands on your own or upgrade to a guided tour to gain more insight into their rich history and significance. The tour guides are knowledgeable and passionate about the islands and will share interesting facts and stories with you.The upgrade option for the double-decker bus tour allows you to explore more of New York City's landmarks and attractions. You can hop on and off the bus at multiple stops throughout the city, including Times Square, the Empire State Building, and the Brooklyn Bridge. You can customize your itinerary, take your time at each stop, and create your own adventure.This tour is perfect for solo travelers, families, or groups of friends who want to experience the rich history and culture of New York City. This tour is a great way to explore the culture, history, and diversity of New York City. With convenient transportation, knowledgeable guides, and incredible views, you'll have an unforgettable experience that will stay with you long after you've left the city. This tour is a must-do for anyone visiting the Big Apple!</p></div>",
