      "name": "VIP ACCESS: Ellis Island, Statue Liberty and Battery Park Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>The VIP ACCESS: Ellis Island, Statue Liberty and Battery Park Walking Tour offers visitors the opportunity to experience some of New York City's most iconic landmarks with VIP access and a knowledgeable guide.The tour begins with a 30-minute guided walking tour of Battery Park, during which your guide will provide you with insight into the park's history and significance. From there, you will be escorted through the Reserve Access Line to the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island Ferry, allowing you to avoid the long lines and save time.Once you arrive on Liberty Island, you will have the opportunity to explore the grounds and enjoy stunning views of the statue. You can also opt to climb to the top of the pedestal or visit the newly opened Statue Museum.After visiting Liberty Island, you will board the ferry once again over to Ellis Island, where you can explore the historic immigration museum and learn about the experiences of the millions of immigrants who passed through its halls.Along the way, you will also get to experience the beautiful Seaglass Carousel, Battery Cannon, Coast Guard Memorial, Bosque Gardens and Fountain, and more.The tour concludes back at the original departure point after approximately 3 hours. Visitors also have the option to upgrade for a fully guided tour or a visit to the new Statue Museum. Ellis Island, Statue Liberty and Battery Park Walking Tour is a fantastic way to experience these iconic landmarks with the added benefits of VIP access and a knowledgeable guide. With personalized guidance and convenient transportation, you can relax and enjoy the sights and sounds of these historic sites.</p></div>",
