      "name": "New York: 20+ Top Manhattan Sights Guided Walking Tour + 9/11 Museum Entry",
      "shortDescription": "Visit the Charging Bull, the Fearless Girl, and learn about the heroes of 9/11",
      "description": "See Manhattan's top 20 landmarks with a local guide, then visit the 9/11 Museum.\r\n\r\nStart on Wall Street, the oldest part of Manhattan. Then, walk through this historic district and see Ground Zero, the Charging Bull, and Fearless Girl at the New York Stock Exchange. Then, move on to City Hall for views of the Brooklyn Bridge and courthouse buildings.\r\n\r\nNext, visit Five Points, Chinatown, and Little Italy. Learn about their cultures and find out where to eat the best local food. End the walking tour near the Flatiron Building.\r\n\r\nThen, go to the 9/11 Museum to learn about the history of the attacks and hear stories of individual and collective heroic actions. The museum features exhibitions commemorating the victims and heroes of the attacks.\r\n\r\nThe tour lasts 5 hours, including 3 hours walking in Manhattan and about 2 hours at the 9/11 Museum. The guide will not join you inside the museum.",
