      "shortDescription": "Day tour to Philadelphia the Amish Country including an Amish buggy Ride",
      "description": "Get ready for an adventure that will take you away from the hustle and bustle of New York to the City of Brotherly Love. Explore iconic Philly landmarks such as the Liberty Bell, Independence National Park, Congress Hall and Elfreth's Alley - the oldest continuously inhabited street in America.\r\n\r\nContinue your journey to the Financial District, Benjamin Franklin Parkway, and other historic sites around the city. As you depart Philadelphia, don't miss the chance to climb the famous \"Rocky Steps\" before heading to Lancaster County, home of the Amish people.\r\n\r\nExperience an authentic Amish Buggy ride through the beautiful Amish farm country and learn about their centuries-old culture that has survived without the benefits of modern technology. Discover how they adapted, using innovative methods to create self-sufficient farms that rely on renewable energy sources. You'll be amazed how much of modern life you take for granted!",
