      "shortDescription": "Explore Wall Street and see the Charging Bull statue",
      "description": "Visit over 20 of New York's famous landmarks, then see the Metropolitan Museum of Art, one of the world's largest and finest art museums.\r\n\r\nStart on Wall Street, Manhattan's oldest area. View notable sites such as Ground Zero and the Charging Bull and Fearless Girl statues at the New York Stock Exchange. Then, walk to City Hall to see the Brooklyn Bridge and the Court Houses.\r\n\r\nNext, go to Five Points, Chinatown, and Little Italy. Learn about these neighborhoods and find tips for great places to eat in NYC. Finish your tour near the Flatiron Building in Midtown.\r\n\r\nAfter the walking tour, go to the Met. It has 500,000 works spanning 5,000 years, from prehistory to now.\r\n\r\nThe tour lasts approximately 5 hours (3 hours for the Manhattan Walking Tour and 2 hours for the Met). The guide does not accompany you inside the museum.",
