      "name": "High Line, Chelsea & Hudson Yards: Guided Walking Tour + Edge NYC Entry Ticket",
      "description": "<div><p>Begin the tour at Little Island, NYC’s new waterfront park, and learn how the city has used its waterfront for growth, industry, and transport.\r</p><p>Walk through the Meatpacking District and Gansevoort Peninsula, areas that have transformed from industrial centers to trendy neighborhoods. \r</p><p>Discover their history, from market days to the creation of the High Line.\r</p><p>Visit Chelsea Market, famous for its food hall and as the birthplace of the Oreo cookie. \r</p><p>Explore Artists and Fleas, a market with unique items. Stroll along the High Line, an elevated park that reflects NYC’s ongoing changes, and hear its story from your guide.\r</p><p>End the tour in Hudson Yards, home to notable buildings like The Vessel and The Shed. \r</p><p>Visit Edge NYC, the highest outdoor sky deck in the Western Hemisphere, to enjoy 360-degree views of the city. The tour ends here, and you can spend some time here at your leisure.</p></div>",
