      "description": "<div><p>The **Metropolitan Museum of Art** is New York’s most valuable landmark with over **2 million artistic masterpieces**, including anything and everything from modern European art, to ancient treasures of Greek and Egyptian antiquity. \r</p><p>Climb the Grand Staircase and enter to admire over 5,000 years of art from around the world. \r</p><p>See the Chicago Stock Exchange at the American Wing, which houses the portrait of *Washington Crossing the Delaware*. Visit the Medieval European Gallery where you will get to see the armor worn by the notorious King Henry VIII. \r</p><p>The Met can take days to explore, but you'll get to scratch the surface with an **expert guide** (if selected) to help you navigate the must-sees and the hidden gems.\r</p><p>Make the most of your trip to the Met with **private tours, small group guided tours or a self-guided tour** that includes a live presentation from Met staff.</p></div>",
