      "name": "New York: Manhattan Guided Walking Tour + Museum of Modern Art Entry",
      "description": "<div><p>Prepare for a tour to see New York's 20+ key landmarks and visit the Museum of Modern Art (MoMA), known for its modern art collection.\r</p><p>Start the tour on Wall Street, the oldest part of Manhattan. See Ground Zero, the Charging Bull, and Fearless Girl at the New York Stock Exchange, and walk to City Hall to view the Brooklyn Bridge.\r</p><p>Continue to the Five Points, Chinatown, and Little Italy. Learn about their cultures and get tips on local NYC food. The tour ends near the Flatiron Building.\r</p><p>After the walking tour, visit MoMA. View works like Van Gogh’s The Starry Night, Monet’s Water Lilies, Warhol’s Campbell’s Soup Cans, Dalí’s The Persistence of Memory, and Wyeth’s Christina’s World. The guide will not accompany you inside MoMA.</p></div>",
