      "name": "New York: 3-Hour Manhattan Guided Walking Tour + One World Observatory Entry",
      "description": "<div><p>See over 20 significant Manhattan landmarks before heading to One World Observatory for views from New York's tallest building.\r</p><p>Start your tour on Wall Street, the oldest part of Manhattan. Then, walk through the financial district and see Ground Zero, the Charging Bull, and the Fearless Girl at the New York Stock Exchange. Reach City Hall to catch glimpses of the Brooklyn Bridge and nearby courthouses.\r</p><p>Afterward, visit Five Points, Chinatown, and Little Italy. Learn about their culture and get tips on the best local food. Conclude the walking tour near the Flatiron Building.\r</p><p>Visit One World Observatory after the walking tour. Take the Sky Pod Elevator to the top, explore three levels, and see 360° views of the New York skyline, extending up to 45 miles.\r</p><p>The tour lasts about five hours: three hours walking in Manhattan and two hours at the Observatory. The guide will not join at the Observatory.</p></div>",
