      "name": "New York: Guided Walking Tour + Staten Island Roundtrip Ferry",
      "description": "<div><p>Prepare for a 5-hour tour to see three major New York's top attractions i.e.; Brooklyn Bridge, the Statue of Liberty, and Manhattan's historical buildings.\r</p><p>Start the tour at York Street Metro Station. Capture photos of the Brooklyn and Manhattan Bridges before heading to Brooklyn Bridge Park, where old warehouses now serve as restaurants and bars.\r</p><p>Visit Brooklyn Heights and its promenade, seen in many films and TV shows. Walk across the Brooklyn Bridge for views of the Manhattan skyline. Afterward, visit Lower Manhattan, including Chinatown, Little Italy, the 9/11 Memorial, Wall Street, and more.\r</p><p>The tour ends at Battery Park, where you can catch a ferry to the Statue of Liberty or Staten Island. The free Staten Island ferry provides a direct view of the Statue of Liberty. Explore Staten Island or return to Battery Park and the guide will not join you on the ferry.</p></div>",
