      "description": "<div><p>Join a New York walking tour to see over 30 top sights with a local guide. Visit the Metropolitan Museum of Art, one of the largest and finest art museums, with 500,000 works spanning 5,000 years of world culture.\r</p><p>Start at Wall Street to see key buildings, Ground Zero, and the NY Stock Exchange, alongside the Charging Bull and Fearless Girl statues. Walk to City Hall and glimpse the Brooklyn Bridge and the Court Houses known for historic trials.\r</p><p>Visit the neighborhoods of 5 Points, Chinatown, and Little Italy. See the Flatiron Building and continue up 5th Avenue for views of the Empire State Building, Chrysler Building, and Bryant Park.\r</p><p>Go to Grand Central Station, Times Square, Rockefeller Center, St. Patrick’s Cathedral, and more. End the tour at the Plaza Hotel.\r</p><p>After the walking tour, visit the Metropolitan Museum of Art to view its extensive collection. Your guide will not accompany you inside the museum.</p></div>",
