      "name": "Statue of Liberty, Ellis Island & 9/11 Memorial: Guided Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Take a guided tour of New York’s most well-known places: the Statue of Liberty, Ellis Island, Wall Street, and the 9/11 Memorial. Choose a guide in English, Spanish, or French, and skip long lines with priority ferry boarding and optionally include entry to the 9/11 Museum. \r</p><p>Start at Battery Park and ride a ferry across to Liberty Island. On Liberty Island, learn the history and powerful symbolism of Lady Liberty, designed by Gustave Eiffel. Take photos from the best spots and enjoy some free time to explore the Statue of Liberty Museum. \r</p><p>Next, go to Ellis Island to hear stories of immigrants into the USA at the Immigration Museum. Return to Battery Park and walk through Wall Street, where you can see the New York Stock Exchange and Federal Hall. \r</p><p>End at Ground Zero to see the Memorial Pools. Upgrade to visit the 9/11 Museum for more artifacts and exhibits.</p></div>",
