      "name": "New York: Midtown Walking Tour + Empire State Building Entry",
      "description": "<div><p>Join a walking tour of Midtown Manhattan to learn about the history, architecture, and energy of New York City. See the Chrysler Building, American Radiator Building, Macy’s, and One Vanderbilt. Hear stories of the changing NYC skyline.\r</p><p>Midtown NYC showcases different architectural styles like Beaux-Arts and Art Deco. Your guide will explain the details and symbols of each, including hidden features like underground tunnels and interesting items inside, such as a turn-of-the-century National Historic Landmark that holds Winnie the Pooh.\r</p><p>Pause in Bryant Park and walk along Fifth Avenue while learning how the \"race to the sky\" changed America. Finish at the Empire State Building, where a ticket allows access to the 86th-floor observatory for a final view of the city.</p></div>",
