      "name": "New York: Brooklyn Bridge & DUMBO Guided Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Start at the Oculus, a modern architectural site. The English-speaking guide will brief you about the tour. After that, walk towards City Hall Park and learn about 19th-century New York and the need to build a bridge that became world famous. At the Brooklyn Bridge entrance, hear about its construction and its significance in engineering. Walk along the pedestrian path for views of the Manhattan skyline and the East River; It's great for photos.\r</p><p>Next, visit DUMBO, a neighborhood known for its creative scene. Walk on cobblestone streets that show its shift from an industrial area to a place with boutiques and galleries. Take photos at Washington Street, where the Manhattan Bridge frames the Empire State Building. Finish at Fulton Ferry Landing, which has food and entertainment options.</p></div>",
