      "name": "New York: Manhattan Guided Walking Tour + Liberty Cruise Ticket",
      "description": "<div><p>Prepare for a tour to see 20+ top New York sights with a local guide, then board a boat cruise with views of the Statue of Liberty, Ellis Island, Governors Island, and more.\r</p><p>The tour starts on Wall St., the oldest part of Manhattan. View the busy district and see Ground Zero and the Charging Bull &amp; Fearless Girl at the New York Stock Exchange. Walk to City Hall to spot the Brooklyn Bridge and famous courthouses.\r</p><p>Visit the Five Points, Chinatown, Little Italy, and learn about their cultures, and receive tips on local NYC food. Finish the tour near the Flatiron Building.\r</p><p>After the walking tour, go to Hudson River Park to board a cruise with city skylines, bridges, and the Statue of Liberty.\r</p><p>The tour consists of a 3-hour Manhattan Walking Tour and 75 minutes on the Liberty Cruise Boat, with a break in between. The guide will not join you on the cruise.</p></div>",
