      "name": "Beacon Hill Boston: Small Group Underground Railroad History Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Step back in time with a stroll down Boston's historic Beacon Hill, the setting of the city's spirited fight against legalized slavery. Embark on the Black Heritage Trail, a walking path that weaves a tale of bravery and resistance. Led by an expert local guide, this 2.5-hour tour takes you from Boston Common to hidden Underground Railroad sites, grand homes of the \"Boston Brahmins,\" and essential abolitionist landmarks like the African Meeting House.\r</p><p>The intimate small-group setting allows an immersive dive into the tumultuous years from 1833 to 1863, a period teetering on the edge of the Civil War. Experience the echoes of 19th-century Bostonians, each wrestling with the morally fraught practice of racial enslavement in the U.S.</p></div>",
