      "description": "<div><p>Meet your guide in Times Square at the statue of George M. Cohan, a monument dedicated to the father of American musical comedy. Follow into the footsteps of theater legends and learn about some of the greats like Ethel Barrymore, Judy Garland, Humphrey Bogart, Julie Andrews and many more. As you explore the Theater District, a Broadway expert will share their own tale of theater dreams. Guides, often professional actors or directors, have extensive knowledge of show business and will make sure to include their personal experiences into the rich historical narrative. What better way to view the bright lights of Broadway than through the eyes of an artist?</p></div>",
