      "name": "Brooklyn Bridge, Statue of Liberty, and Manhattan Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>This 5-hour tour lets you see and experience the three big attractions in NYC. Brooklyn BridgeStatue of Liberty Manhattan and its historical &amp; iconic buildings and sightsYou will start at York Street Metro Station in Brooklyn’s trendy Dumbo neighborhood, at the foot of the world-famous Brooklyn Bridge – a great spot to get a photo of both the Brooklyn and Manhattan Bridges.After a quick introduction from your guide, we head to Brooklyn Bridge Park under the Brooklyn Bridge, where civil war era warehouses have been turned into vibrant restaurants and bars.You continue to Brooklyn Heights and the promenade – made famous by many movies and TV Shows. After our quick tour of Brooklyn, we start our walk across the Brooklyn Bridge. This is where we will see the best views of the Manhattan skyline, so keep your camera handy!Once you have crossed over the bridge you head into Lower Manhattan. You will see a lot in this area; China Town, Little Italy, 5 points, 9/11 memorial, Ground Zero, Woolworth Building, City Hall, Wall St &amp; The NY Stock Exchange, and much more!The last stop is Battery Park. Located on the southern tip of Manhattan, this is where the ferries and boats arrive to take passengers to the Statue of Liberty &amp; Staten Island.The 30-minute Staten Island ferry is free to all to use and it gives incredible views of The Statue of Liberty. Once you arrive at Staten Island, feel free to explore or you can simply take the ferry back to Battery Park.</p></div>",
