      "name": "9-11 Memorial and Ground Zero Tour with Museum Access",
      "description": "<div><p>Embark on a moving journey through New York City, where stories of resilience, heroism, and renewal come to life. Begin at St. Paul’s Chapel, a sanctuary of hope after 9/11. Led by a local expert, you’ll discover the profound significance of this site, setting the stage for an unforgettable exploration of courage and recovery.As you approach the Oculus, Santiago Calatrava’s architectural masterpiece, witness a symbol of New York’s rebirth. This futuristic hub stands as a testament to the city’s enduring spirit, uniting people in a vibrant centre of connectivity.Pay tribute to the brave souls at the FDNY Memorial at Engine 10/Ladder 10, the closest fire station to Ground Zero. Your guide will share stories of bravery and sacrifice, bringing to life the firefighters’ heroic response. Continue to the 9/11 Memorial, where the Reflecting Absence twin pools honour those lost, with your guide explaining the powerful symbolism of this space.Visit St. Peter’s Church and the Survivor Tree, a living symbol of hope that survived the devastation. Discover St. Peter’s role as a refuge, and explore Brookfield Place and the Winter Garden Atrium, both key in the area’s recovery.</p></div>",
