      "name": "The ultimate Brooklyn guided bike tour",
      "description": "<div><p>See some of New York City’s most famous sights while working up a sweat on this exciting sightseeing comprehensive bike tour. Begin on the Lower East Side of Manhattan, once the most densely populated neighborhood in the world, now a very hip area with a thriving nightlife and plenty of quirks. Then delve into Brooklyn with the high-end trendy, and colorful neighborhood of Williamsburg, you will visit Domino Park, where the sugar refining industry of the past comes to life with all sorts of devices that surround you and play with your senses.And if that is not enough, see building sized street murals that you will swear must be photographs but are actually hand painted projects by local artists. From iconic bridges to waterfront views, and the coolest streets, this tour finds thrills for everyone as it balances serenity with excitement.As travel through time, you will pass by the Brooklyn Navy Yard, site of nearly 200 years of ship building history and the birthplace of scores of famous ships, from the Fulton Steam Frigate to the USS Maine!Complete and return to the 21st century as ride to the now-posh neighborhood of DUMBO and finally pedal over the Brooklyn Bridge to take in incredible views of the New York skyline and harbor.</p></div>",
