      "name": "Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island private guided tour",
      "description": "<div><p>See New York through a different perspective on a private tour to visit both the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island. Discover the history of US immigration and the persons who helped grow the wealth and history of the United States.It is estimated that forty per cent of the entire US population can trace at least one relative's arrival in the US, through the port of New York and Ellis Island. At Ellis Island, you will learn the many extraordinary stories of families journeying to New York City since the earliest days of the United States' founding. Begin at Castle Clinton, a former Fort in Battery Park, where you will board the ferry to the famous Liberty Island. Along the way, you will learn about the remarkable history of the Statue.Outside the Statue of Liberty Museum and the Ellis Island Immigration Museum, your guide will give you full information on each island. Then, they will silently accompany you through the museums, which you can enjoy at your own pace. Immerse yourself in the immigrant's journey through Ellis Island.Your tour will end on Ellis Island, where you can choose to return with your guide to Battery Park. </p></div>",
