      "name": "Discover NY Tour glass-top bus tour with cruise",
      "description": "<div><p>Explore New York City aboard of a glass-top bus for an unforgettable journey through the city that never sleeps! You will see spectacular views of iconic NYC landmarks on board luxury climate-controlled buses for an enjoyable all-weather experience. After a drive through the Times Square area, the first stop is at Central Park. The stop includes a short, guided walk into Central Park and a visit to Columbus Circle – one of NYC’s hottest neighbourhoods and the official zero-mile point from which all official city distances are measured. You will also pass through the shops at Columbus Circle at Deutsche Bank Centre, the Museum of Arts and Design, and the famous Plaza Hotel. Rockefeller Centre.The second stop is Rockefeller Centre, where beautiful views over St. Patrick’s Cathedral await. You’ll also see the location of the winter ice-skating rink and Christmas Tree, and NBC’s Today Show set. 5th Avenue and Empire State Building Views.The third stop is on Fifth Avenue, where you pause to admire the iconic Empire State Building. The tour also passes by Madison Square Park – the original location of Madison Square Garden Arena, and continues with a drive through iconic NYC neighbourhoods such as Greenwich Village, Soho, Chinatown, and the Financial District.En route to the fourth stop, you continue to Wall Street for views of the New York Stock Exchange, Federal Hall (the location of the first Capitol Building of the United States), Trinity Church, and the famous Charging Bull sculpture on Broadway. World Trade Center and 9/11 Memorial. The next stop is the World Trade Center, where you visit the 9/11 Memorial. Around 1 pm, you’ll stop for a quick lunch break (not included on the price) at Gansevoort Liberty Market. (Lunch is not included on your tour).The fifth stop is the Whitehall Terminal in downtown Manhattan, for a boat ride on the Staten Island ferry. During your relaxing cruise, soak up magnificent views over the Statue of Liberty to the Manhattan and Brooklyn skyline beyond. The boat docks back at the Whitehall Terminal, where the local partner board the bus to head back to the original departure point on 7th Avenue in the Times Square area. The tour concludes at 3 PM and 4 PM, back where it began.</p></div>",
