      "name": "Two-Day Tour to Niagara Falls, Washington D.C., and Philadelphia",
      "description": "<div><p>On this 2-day tour, you'll first journey by motor coach to the Niagara Falls, traversing the landscape of up state New York. Upon arrival, you'll step aboard the historic Maid of the Mist boat cruise or explore from other vantage points such as the Cave of the Winds Gorge Walk. Here, you'll delve into the history of these mighty waters and take in the views from various perspectives. After a day filled with wonder, you'll return to Manhattan's Times Square, arriving back between 11pm-midnight.Two days later, you'll depart from Times Square, heading south to two of America’s historical capitals. Your first stop is Washington D.C., where your exploration begins at the Iwo Jima Memorial, a tribute to the US Marines. From there, you'll visit the Lincoln Memorial before taking in an exterior view of two pillars of U.S. government: the White House and the Capitol Building. You'll have some free time for lunch before setting off for your next destination.Up next is Philadelphia, PA, the first ever U.S. capital chosen during the Revolutionary War. On arrival, you'll be guided through Philadelphia's Old City neighbourhood and the Independence National Historical Park. Here, you'll see iconic sites like the Liberty Bell and Independence Hall, where America's founding documents were debated and adopted. The tour concludes with a stop at the Rocky Steps in front of the Philadelphia Museum of Art, offering you a chance to re-enact a classic movie scene by ascending to the top.</p></div>",
