      "description": "<div><p>Step back into the 1930s and explore the Rockefeller Center, often referred to as a \"city within a city\". This Art Deco masterpiece transports you to an era of grandeur and creativity, revealing the artistic influence of Ancient Greece and more contemporary times.Embark on a journey through the heart of this historic site with your guide. Visit iconic landmarks such as the renowned Radio City Music Hall and the legendary 30 Rock, home to “Saturday Night Live”. And the scene at the Rockefeller Center is ever-changing. In summer, the Channel Gardens burst with seasonal blooms, while during Christmas, it's impossible to resist capturing a photo against the famous evergreen tree. Your guide will be more than happy to assist with photography!If you select the option with Top of the Rock included, you'll conclude your tour by ascending over 800 feet to three levels of observatory views. From here, you can admire Manhattan from above with spectacular 360-degree views, both indoors and outdoors.</p></div>",
