      "name": "Fast track 4-hour Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Meet your guide in Battery Park, where you’ll board a ferry for Liberty Island with special tickets that help you avoid long lines. Explore the grounds with an expert guide who shares details about the Statue of Liberty’s history and construction, and get a preview of what awaits inside the new museum. Take time afterward to explore the museum at your own pace, viewing artifacts like the statue’s original iron framework and one of its early torch flames.</p><p>Hop back on the ferry to Ellis Island, the gateway for millions of immigrants between 1892 and 1954. Your guide highlights notable points on the island, such as The Wall of Honor, before giving you tips on what to see in the Museum of Immigration. Enjoy free time to dive deeper into these exhibits, listen to moving stories via an included audio guide, and even research your own family’s history.</p></div>",
