      "name": "Self-guided audio tour of New York's iconic sights in Manhattan",
      "description": "<div><p>Join this in-app audio tour to experience one of the best parts of Manhattan, and make your time in New York memorable. You will sense the spirit of this great city and see its diversity while walking through the most famous places of the northern part of Manhattan and a little of its central portion.Start the tour enjoying the quietness and beauty of Central Park, and then lose yourself among the skyscrapers like the Trump Tower, the city's symbol of wealth, and the Empire State Building, the tallest building in New York. Next, this tour will bring you to the famous Museum Mile. Choose to visit the Metropolitan Museum of Art, which is often compared to the Louvre, the Guggenheim Museum housed inside one of the most famous buildings on the planet, and other museums. You will learn how the genre of the Broadway musical emerged, the places New Yorkers like to meet and sit, and the mistake on the fresco at the Grand Terminal Station.Your must-do will be to walk on 5th Avenue, an elegant, legendary, longest, and most expensive street in the city, and to come to Times Square visited by millions of people over the course of the year. Last but not least, you will arrive to the Dakota, a well-known building where John Lennon and Yoko Ono lived their happy moments until a crime that shocked the entire world occurred.</p></div>",
