      "name": "Half-day guided bus tour of New York City's landmarks",
      "description": "<div><p>Embark on a half-day exploration of New York City's highlights, comfortably seated in a climate-controlled bus. Accompanied by a local guide, you'll have the opportunity to capture photos at four iconic locations while enjoying the cityscape.Your adventure begins at the giant Button and Needle statue, situated near Times Square on W 39th Street and 7th Avenue. From this point, journey through Midtown as your guide points out landmarks such as Radio City Music Hall and Central Park, sharing fun stories and movie trivia along the way. You'll gain insights into John Lennon’s life in NYC as you pass by the Dakota Building, before heading towards the elegant Plaza Hotel and opulent Fifth Avenue. Pause for photographs at Rockefeller Center, followed by a drive past the Empire State Building, Flatiron Building, and Washington Square Arch.The tour proceeds through SoHo, Chinatown, and the Financial District, with a photo stop at Pier 17 to view the Brooklyn Bridge. Pay a visit to the 9/11 Memorial and take in views of the Statue of Liberty from the land. Conclude your journey with sights of Chelsea Piers and Hudson Yards, ending near Macy’s, conveniently located close to subways, dining options, and shopping outlets. This tour offers an ideal way to experience NYC in half a day, combining relaxation and sightseeing.</p></div>",
