      "name": "Grand Central Terminal and Manhattan Sights Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Discover the best of New York’s Manhattan district and see over 20 of the city’s most iconic landmarks with a fun local guide, then visit the world-famous Grand Central Terminal to explore its renowned spots, including the iconic Grand Central Terminal Clock.The tour begins on the world-famous Wall Street, the oldest part of Manhattan. Soak up the unique atmosphere of this busy district, and see some of the city’s most recognizable sights including Ground Zero and The Charging Bull at the New York Stock ExchangeContinue to Five Points, Chinatown, and Little Italy. Learn about the vibrant culture of these neighbourhoods and the people who live here as well as tips on the best local places to eat some amazing food.After the tour, enjoy a break for lunch (not included) before exploring Grand Central Terminal on a guided tour to see all its memorable attractions. Grand Central Terminal boasts over 150 years of history, featuring numerous locations popularized in films and television. Highlights of this historic tour include the transformed movie theater now serving as a wine store, the renowned oyster bar, and The New York Transit Museum.The tour is approximately 6 hours in duration (3 hours Manhattan Walking Tour and approximately 1.5 hours at the Grand Central Terminal Tour, with a break in between. Your walking tour guide will not accompany you inside the Grand Central Terminal, but you’ll be joined by an official station tour guide)</p></div>",
