      "name": "Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island Guided Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Discover the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island on a guided tour.Start your journey at Battery Park, where you'll gather with fellow travellers and enjoy breathtaking views of the New York Harbor and the Statue of Liberty. Your English-speaking guide will offer an engaging introduction to the significance of the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island, setting the stage for an unforgettable experience.Board the ferry to Liberty Island, where you'll marvel at the Statue of Liberty and the Manhattan skyline. Your guide will share captivating stories about the Statue, a gift from France symbolizing freedom and democracy. Explore the island, learn about the statue’s design and construction, and take time to capture stunning photographs.Next, sail to Ellis Island, the historic gateway for over 12 million immigrants. Visit the Ellis Island Immigration Museum to discover exhibits that chronicle the immigrant experience and the history of U.S. immigration. Your guide’s narratives will bring to life the diverse stories of those who passed through Ellis Island, offering a poignant look at their trials, hopes, and dreams.Return to Battery Park with the option to explore further or head back with your guide. Enjoy the scenic ride and reflect on the deep significance of the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island as symbols of hope and new beginnings. This tour ensures you gain a profound understanding of these iconic landmarks and their impact on American heritage.</p></div>",
