      "name": "Brownstone Brooklyn guided food tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Discover the culinary delights of Brooklyn's Smith and Court Streets, a neighbourhood renowned for its eclectic mix of small, locally owned, artisanal food shops. This food tour offers an insight into how these distinctive establishments came to be and what sets them apart. Guided by a local expert, you'll explore a diverse range of cuisines.The tour showcases the best of Brooklyn's gastronomic offerings, celebrating those who elevate cuisine to an art form. You'll visit long-established haunts as well as innovative new culinary ventures, sampling a dynamic menu of both traditional flavours and daring dishes. The itinerary includes stops at Italian and Middle Eastern shops that have been neighbourhood staples for years, along with a growing number of cafes and restaurants specialising in New American cuisine.As you savour the delicacies, you'll also learn about the rich history and evolving character of the neighbourhood. From bread shops and Italian pastry stores to cafes boasting their own coffee roasters and the city's oldest Middle Eastern bakery, this corner of Brooklyn is truly one-of-a-kind. Its shops and food have garnered international attention, featuring in press and television coverage worldwide. However, despite their fame, some original businesses have struggled against the challenges facing small business owners in New York. The tour provides insights into these struggles and discusses ways to continue supporting these establishments.</p></div>",
