      "name": "High Line, Chelsea, Hudson Yards Walking Tour with Edge Admission",
      "description": "<div><p>Experience the dynamic evolution of New York City on this immersive tour! Begin at Little Island, a stunning new waterfront park, where your guide will reveal how NYC’s waterfront has driven its growth—think industry, transportation, and constant transformation.Next, explore the Meatpacking District and Gansevoort Peninsula, once gritty industrial hubs, now hotspots of art, fashion, and innovation. Learn how this neighborhood played a key role in shaping NYC’s identity, from bustling markets to the iconic High Line railroad.Then, dive into Chelsea Market, a vibrant food hall known for its culinary history, including being the birthplace of the Oreo cookie. Browse through Artists and Fleas for unique local treasures before stepping onto the High Line, an elevated park showcasing New York’s urban renewal. As you walk, enjoy stunning views and hear the fascinating history behind this green oasis.The tour culminates at Hudson Yards, a glimpse into NYC’s future, with its cutting-edge architecture, including The Vessel and The Shed. Finally, you’ll ascend to Edge, the highest outdoor sky deck in the Western Hemisphere, where 360-degree views of the city will leave you speechless.This tour is perfect for those eager to explore the past, present, and future of New York City.</p></div>",
