      "description": "<div><p>Explore four of New York City's boroughs from the comfort of your bus with and entertaining expert guide! You will meet your guide in the heart of Manhattan near Times Square and you will get onboard your air-conditioned bus and head north to the historic Harlem neighborhood. After a stop at the Apollo Theater Walk of Fame, you will continue north into the Bronx, the birthplace of hip hop and rap and home to the New York Yankees, where you could also see incredible graffiti murals.Later you will discover the Queens, the largest borough of New York City. There, you will visit Flushing Meadow-Corona Park, you will then head to Brooklyn, home of street art and graffiti murals and also a foodie destination, so you could take a break and grab some food.You will also visit the Williamsburg Hasidic Jewish community and experience their distinct shops, fashion and eateries. As you leave Brooklyn, you will be able to admire the beautiful Brooklyn bridge and enjoy the Manhattan skyline. The tour will end in Manhattan's Little Italy and Chinatown, where you could wander, do some shopping and eating, or stay for dinner.</p></div>",
