      "name": "Statue of Liberty and Immigration Museum Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Embark on an unforgettable journey to Ellis Island, where millions of immigrants passed through between 1892 and 1924 in pursuit of the \"American Dream.\" This iconic location tells the stories of hope, resilience, and new beginnings that shaped the United States.Your experience will be guided by an expert tour leader, who will provide fascinating insights and ensure you're fully prepared to explore. While regulations may prevent them from guiding inside certain areas, you'll receive an audio guide packed with all the essential information to make the most of your visit.Choose the option that best suits your style, and please make sure to note which option you have selected:<strong>Basic Option</strong>: Ideal for independent explorers! Receive ferry tickets and an interactive audio guide to enjoy at your own pace.<strong>Classic Guided Option</strong>: Perfect for those who love learning from a local expert. Follow your guide to Liberty Island and Ellis Island for live storytelling (museum guidance not included).<strong>Premium Option</strong>: The ultimate experience! Enjoy the best of both worlds with a guided tour and a handy audio guide to dive deeper, even in areas where the guide can't provide explanations such as inside the museums or on the ferry during peak times.Whether you're exploring on your own or with a guide, this tour is a must for anyone looking to connect with the rich culture and history of New York City. Book now and let history come to life!</p></div>",
