      "name": "East Village Ice Cream Crawl // Lower East Side",
      "description": "Discover a different side to a city on an immersive food walk and market tours. Our local hosts will show you all their favorite places to eat, drink and have fun!<br><br>Toasted Sesame Nutella. Salty Caramel. Honey Comb. Cereal Milk. Peppermint Chocolate. Brooklyn Brown Sugar Chunk. Thai Iced Tea. Earl Gray Tea. Oreo Cookie Dough. Cake Batter. Ginger. \n\nWe stop at six different world-class New York City ice cream shops on this 1.5 mile 1.5 hour tour. At each ice cream store we'll explore the story behind the business and see what makes these frozen desserts unique as you savor every flavor. You'll learn about an ex drug dealer who turned his life around through culinary creativity, an ice cream shop that's been passed down in a family through generations, and a translator who found her real calling. A picture is worth a thousand words, but a scoop of ice cream tells a story.\n\nWhile exploring the East Village we hit the best ice cream shops and taste no fewer than 12 flavors based on a mix of my experience and your interest.",
