      "name": "Local & Seasonal Cooking Class  | Greenwich Village",
      "description": "Join the latest culinary trend of immersive and social dining where local hosts invite you into their homes for a magical meal.<br><br>Discover fresh seasonal cooking with host Mary in her Greenwich Village home with amazing skyline views! In this hands-on cooking class, you'll learn the techniques and ingredients that make cooking and shopping locally so healthy and delicious. This is a true farm-to-table class - Mary shops from the Union Square farmer's market where are the best NYC restaurant chef's shop. But since hacking a butternut squash or what to do with ingredients like fennel or pak choi can seem daunting, Mary will guide you through each step of the cooking process with expert tips and tricks. With a focus on plant-based ingredients, and recipes that change with the seasons, this class is perfect for anyone looking to explore new and delicious cooking. Whether you're an experienced cook or a beginner, you'll leave this class feeling inspired and empowered to create your own farmer's market inspired dishes at home, plus you'll take home some granola that you learn to make! Book your spot in Mary's cooking class today for a one-of-a-kind culinary experience!\n\nAperitif Served. Guests can BYOB!",
