      "name": "Pasta Cooking Class & Multi-course Italian Dinner // Greenwich Village ",
      "description": "What better way to explore a city than by discovering its cuisine first hand? Put on a chef's hat for the day and learn how to make classic dishes, local specialties and impressive plates with our expert hosts. Sign up for one of our fun, immersive cooking classes and discover a new hidden talent!<br><br>Cook with a NYC local that grew up Italian and has been cooking Italian food her entire life. Mary is an expert at jarring tomatoes, making fresh pasta and sauces like pesto, marina, Cacio e Pepe and clam sauce. You will learn these new recipes at this Greenwich Village home with lovely skyline views and may be able to dine on the roof. This is a hands-on class, but customizable for those that would prefer to take more notes and enjoy the sit down meal. Most of the ingredients are purchased from the Union Square Farmer's Market where all the best NYC Chefs shop. ",
