      "name": "New York City Sightseeing Bus Tour from Manhattan",
      "description": "<div><p>Begin your in-depth exploration of New York City in Midtown Manhattan, where you’ll board a comfortable, climate-controlled bus. Your journey begins with a drive through Times Square, followed by a walk in Central Park to see Strawberry Fields and The Dakota—John Lennon’s former residence.</p><p>Back on the bus, pass landmarks like Carnegie Hall, St. Patrick’s Cathedral, Rockefeller Center, and iconic Fifth Avenue, with a glimpse of the Empire State Building rising above. Cruise through Greenwich Village, SoHo, and Chinatown, and take in views of the Flatiron Building from Madison Square Park.</p><p>Stop for lunch at Gansevoort Liberty Market (own expense), then pay your respects at the 9/11 Memorial. Afterward, board the Staten Island Ferry for panoramic views of Manhattan’s skyline, the Statue of Liberty, and Ellis Island.</p><p>Return to Midtown Manhattan, finishing your tour with a richer understanding of the city’s history, architecture, and diverse neighborhoods.</p></div>",
