      "name": "New York City & The High Line - Self Guided Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Join us on our immersive audio tour as we explore New York City’s contemporary developments, history of vintage railways, art deco and contemporary construction.</p><p>Listen to an expert historian guide you through New York City’s stories of the industry, immigration and investment, which can all be seen from one walk along the High Line. Discover the fascinating history rooted in urban transformation and railway networks that are behind the city’s most iconic key attractions.</p><p>We’ll visit some of New York’s best sights, including Chelsea Market, the Flyover, Hudson Yards and the Vessel while also finding out the best places to shop, eat and drink along the High Line. </p><p>Unravel the beauty of New York, learning about the tales, mysteries and secret stories that live on in this cosmopolitan city, to cap off this cultural adventure in this must-see picturesque city.</p><p>Note: This is a self-guided audio walking tour and does not include entrance tickets</p></div>",
