      "name": "NOW OPEN:The Edge Observation Deck Rockefeller Times Square & Hudson Yard Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Meet your friendly guide at the iconic Rockefeller Center, best known as the location for its dazzling Christmas tree which can be seen from November to New Year. Visit Rockefeller’s Central Plaza, which is home to the city’s beloved ice rink during winter months, and converts into a popular outdoor café in summer. Wander around the center and learn about its rich-history and significance to the city along the way, then stop to admire the Rockefeller fountains, which are decorated with seasonal floral displays.</p><p>Walk towards Hudson Yards next, one of the largest private real estate developments in the history of the United States. Learn about and explore this up and coming district then visit The Edge, the highest outdoor sky deck in the Western Hemisphere, boasting a one-of-a-kind design. Suspended mid-air to give the feeling of floating in the sky, The Edge’s viewing deck offers 360 degree views of the city that will leave you breathless. </p></div>",
