      "description": "<div><p>Join Kenny Bollwerk — social media creator and founder of viral “Rat Tok” — for a one-of-a-kind walking tour that shines a light on the city’s most notorious (and furry) residents: the rats.</p><p>As featured in national media and followed by hundreds of thousands online, Kenny leads guests through NYC's backstreets, alleyways, and trash-lined curbs to explore the quirky, grimy, and oddly fascinating world of NYC's rodent population.</p><p>This is part urban adventure, part comedy show, and part public service announcement — all rolled into a 90-minute experience that’s as unforgettable as the city itself.</p><p>Typical Tour</p><p>Insightful (and hilarious) commentary on rat behavior, city infrastructure, rat locations and urban myths.</p><p>Tips on how NYC is fighting its rodent problem — and what still needs to be done</p><p>Perfect for: adventurous tourists, NYC locals, curious animal lovers, and anyone who enjoys learning weird things in weird places.</p></div>",
