      "name": "Art Deco and Architecture Midtown Landmarks Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Spend 2.5 hours discovering midtown Manhattan’s Art Deco wonders and other key landmarks on this small-group walking tour. Join a knowledgeable guide who reveals insider tales behind the city’s iconic buildings and interiors, illustrated with historic photos. Stop into stunning Art Deco lobbies—perfect for cooling off in summer or warming up in winter—and soak up details you might otherwise miss on your own.</p><p>Expect to see and learn about:\n• Bryant Park\n\n• New York Public Library\n\n• American Radiator Building\n\n• 500 5th Avenue\n\n• Bowery Savings Bank Building\n\n• Chanin Building\n\n• Chrysler Building\n\n• Grand Central Terminal\n\n• Rockefeller Center\n\n• And more!</p><p>With fewer people in your group, you’ll have more personal interaction with your guide and plenty of chances to capture unforgettable photos. This tour lets you dive deeper into the architecture and history of midtown, whether it’s your first visit or you’re a seasoned New Yorker.</p></div>",
