      "name": "World Trade Center 911 and Ground Zero Walking Tour in NYC",
      "description": "<div><p>Check in near Broadway, where you’ll be introduced to a captain from the New York City Fire Department—your guide for the day. Begin with an elevated lookout that showcases the World Trade Center Memorial Plaza, revealing One World Trade Center, the 9/11 Museum, and the Reflecting Pools.</p><p>Continue to the World Financial Center, where you’ll uncover the details of Operation Aegis, recognized as the largest maritime evacuation ever conducted. Walk on to the Winter Garden and the Eleven Tears Memorial, each revealing intimate 9/11 stories and insights from your guide that would be easy to overlook on your own.</p><p>Finally, arrive at the World Trade Center complex, layered with further reflections on the day’s events. If you’ve chosen museum tickets, take your time exploring The National 9/11 Memorial &amp; Museum. For those opting for the One World Observatory Package, ascend to the 100th floor for sweeping panoramas of the city below.</p></div>",
