      "name": "High Line, Greenwich Village Food, and Historical Downtown Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Begin your day with a scenic walk along the High Line, an elevated railway turned urban oasis that revitalized Manhattan’s west side. After soaking up the skyline views and art installations, head over to Greenwich Village—long known as a haven for artists, writers, and musicians. Stroll among the historic brownstones and enjoy a specially curated tasting menu, from top-rated pizza to a classic butcher shop, providing you with a memorable lunch.</p><p>Next, venture downtown to uncover the origins of New York City. Wander through the very streets that transformed a humble Dutch fur-trading post into a bustling metropolis of soaring skyscrapers and neon-lit avenues. Your guide’s insights bring to life centuries of history, tying together this comprehensive 5.5-hour experience that weaves together parks, food, and heritage into one fascinating day.</p></div>",
