      "name": "New York City Statue of Liberty Tall Ship Sailing Cruise",
      "description": "<div><p>Set sail in New York City Harbor on board the Clipper City. This unique sightseeing voyage explores the waters of New York City with outstanding views of the Big Apple’s best attractions.</p><p>The original Clipper City was built as a lumber-hauling cargo schooner just before the start of the Civil War. It was then rebuilt from the original plans, which were on loan from the Smithsonian Institution, and more recently refurbished to the modern-day sailing vessel for this tour. The new and improved Clipper City is 158 feet (47 meters) long and 120 feet (36 meters ) high and can accommodate 130 passengers, more than any other sailboat of its kind in the United States. </p><p>Make your way to Pier 17 at South Street Seaport before your cruise departure time. Board the ship, then sit back on one of two decks, and enjoy the views, including the Brooklyn Bridge, Statue of Liberty, Ellis Island, and more. Drinks are available for purchase from the onboard bar. You'll also get the change to help raise or lower the sails, steer or man the ship.</p></div>",
