      "name": "New York Catacombs by Candlelight",
      "description": "<div><p>Begin your 90-minute guided tour at the Basilica of St. Patrick’s Old Cathedral in Lower Manhattan, where you’ll gain rare access to two walled cemeteries normally closed to the public. Learn how this storied church has stood for over two centuries, bearing witness to the evolving Catholic community in New York City and preserving relics of its past.</p><p>Descend beneath the cathedral into the ancient catacombs, closed to outsiders for generations. Here, bishops share the space with prominent New Yorkers who played influential roles in religious and national history. As your guide brings these underground chambers to life with fascinating tales and historical context, you’ll gain a deep appreciation for the enduring legacy—and silent testimonies—of those who rest in this remarkable place.</p></div>",
