      "name": "New York City Harlem Wednesday Morning Tour with Gospel Choir",
      "description": "<div><p>Begin your morning at a central location near Times Square, where you’ll board a comfortable bus to Harlem. Along the way, pass by stately homes and historic buildings, getting a glimpse of the neighborhood’s cultural past and present. See musical landmarks such as the Apollo Theater—where legends of jazz and R&amp;B honed their craft—and stop at the Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture, a national research library dedicated to preserving the experiences of African-descended communities.</p><p>Then, join a local congregation for a stirring morning service, uplifted by the powerful harmonies of the Harlem Gospel Acapella Choir. Conclude your day with a convenient drop-off back near your starting point in the afternoon.</p></div>",
