      "name": "New York of Hamilton the Musical Small-Group Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Begin your three-hour walking tour at the Staten Island Ferry Terminal in Lower Manhattan and set off on a journey guided by the 46 songs of Lin-Manuel Miranda’s <em>Hamilton</em>. Follow in the footsteps of Founding Father Alexander Hamilton, discovering both key events from the musical and real-life locations that played vital roles in his story—whether they appear in the show or not.</p><p>Cover approximately 1.75 miles (2.8 km) on foot, pausing at each significant site to learn about the historical context and sing (or hum) along, if you’d like. From Kings College (<em>Aaron Burr, Sir</em> / <em>My Shot</em>), to the open space once known as the New York City Commons (<em>Right Hand Man</em>), the Federal Reserve (<em>Ten Duel Commandments</em>), and Thomas Jefferson’s onetime residence (<em>The Room Where It Happens</em>), you’ll step into actual places that shaped Hamilton’s political and personal life.</p><p>You’ll also visit the Bank of New York (<em>Take a Break</em>), Federal Hall (<em>Cabinet Battles</em>, <em>Washington On Your Side</em>), the site of Golden Hill (<em>Guns and Ships</em>), Bowling Green (<em>The Reynolds Pamphlet</em>, <em>It’s Quiet Uptown</em>), and Trinity Church (<em>Best of Wives and Best of Women</em>). Along the way, uncover how Hamilton first met George Washington, what led to his fatal duel with Aaron Burr, and the circumstances surrounding his scandalous liaison with Maria Reynolds. Plus, explore Lin-Manuel Miranda’s creative process and gain an insider’s look at how the musical became a Tony-winning phenomenon.</p></div>",
