      "description": "<div><p>Visit one of New York City’s iconic boroughs on a private walking tour. Your guide will meet you in Manhattan, where you will then cross the over-one-mile long bridge on its pedestrian path. Once in Brooklyn, your guide will take you through the DUMBO (‘down under Manhattan Bridge overpass’) neighbourhood, to snap the iconic picture of the bridge through old industrial buildings. Then you’ll get to see some of the borough’s historic industrial past and explore how gentrification has changed the area into one thriving community. Your tour will end in the Time Out Market, where your guide will show you several of their favourite stalls, before departing with you. We encourage you to stay and enjoy a meal, while mixing with the locals. </p></div>",
