      "name": "New York 9/11 Memorial and Ground Zero Private Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Meet your personal guide just outside St. Paul’s Chapel, a church that transformed into a key refuge for rescue teams and mourners immediately following the 9/11 attacks. Explore the memorials within this historic chapel, and hear first-hand stories about the deeply emotional role it played in the aftermath. Continue on to visit the National 9/11 Memorial, pausing at Brookfield Place (formerly the World Financial Center) and the Fireman’s Memorial, where you’ll gain a deeper appreciation for the resilience and heroism that defined New York City at its darkest hour. Stand by the peaceful reflecting pools, set on the Twin Towers’ original footprint, and read some of the nearly 3,000 names inscribed in memory of those who lost their lives.</p><p>For an even more immersive experience, you can opt to head up to One World Observatory. Glide past the typical entry lines and zoom up 100 floors in seconds on a super-speed elevator. Once there, you’ll take in Manhattan’s skyline from 1,250 feet (365 meters) high, and, if you’re feeling brave, step onto the Sky Portal’s transparent floor for a unique look at the streets below.</p></div>",
