      "name": "NYC: Holiday Walking Tour with optional Bryant Park Skating",
      "description": "<div><p>Explore the best of 5th Avenue with an expert local tour guide who will help you discover why New York during the Holiday Season is one of the most magical places on earth. Finish up at Bryant Park Winter Village where you can also choose to go skating on the outdoor rink. </p><p>See the iconic Christmas windows at Bergdorf Goodman, Saks, Cartier, Tiffany and more. Discover the stories behind the Rockefeller Center, as well as the legendary ice rink and the Channel Gardens with their rows of Angels. </p><p>See other sites along the way such as the Plaza Hotel (featured in “Home Alone 2”), St Patrick's Cathedral (New York’s Parish Church) Radio City Music Hall (home to the world famous Rockettes and the Christmas Spectacular Show) and New York Library (with it’ famous Lions) </p><p>The tour finishes at Bryant Park to explore the seasonal Winter Village where you can shop and eat, and even skate on the outdoor skating rink (if you have purchased this option). </p></div>",
