      "description": "<div><p>We start the tour at 8:00 am from your hotel in Manhattan, from Battery Park to Central Park 59th Street with lots of information about the Counties, venture into the Bronx, the beating heart of New York's diversity, Yankee Stadium, Civic Center and the legendary police station \"El Fuerte Apache\".</p><p>and the vibrant graffiti of the Bronx to the elegant residences of Queens. Capture eternal moments in Flushing Meadows, an icon of history and sport, witness to the US Open Tennis and the historic World Fairs.</p><p>Discover Brooklyn, from the Orthodox Jewish community and the vibrant DUMBO, ending at the ferry station. Here embark on an unforgettable journey to the majestic Statue of Liberty. While sailing, you can admire the impressive views of New Jersey, the historic Governor's Island, Brooklyn and the imposing Verrazano Bridge, you will pass near Ellis Island, a site full of history where nearly 12 million immigrants entered the USA.</p></div>",
