      "name": "Upper and Lower Manhaattan Half-Day Bus Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Make your way to the meeting point and meet your guide between 8:30am. Climb aboard the tour vehicle, and head to the west side of Central Park to see the building where John Lennon lived and was murdered, then take in the Strawberry Fields monument to his life. </p><p>Continue past the world’s largest cathedral and Columbia University, see Harlem’s distinctive architecture, and head to the other side of Central Park to cruise down Fifth Avenue. You’ll have views of some of New York’s most famous museums on “Museum Row,” then pass New York touchstones like the Plaza Hotel, Bergdorf Goodman, Trump Tower, and Tiffany’s. </p><p>Keep heading south through NoHo and Soho to see New York at its most fashionable, and explore the traditional immigrant enclaves of Little Italy and Chinatown. Drive into the heart of Wall Street and the Financial District, then learn about the tragic events of 9/11 at Ground Zero, where you’ll also see the rebuilt Freedom Tower. Pull out your camera for a stop in Battery Park, with views across the water to the Statue of Liberty, before returning to Midtown, where this tour concludes.</p></div>",
