      "name": "Guided tour of the MET in Spanish (Metropolitan Museum of Art)",
      "description": "<div><p>Explore the MET with an art history expert and official guide from New York.</p><p>Immerse yourself in 5,000 years of history with a 2-hour Spanish tour of the most important galleries, enjoying the explanations of the main works and avoiding getting lost among their vast collections.</p><p>On this exclusive guided tour, let yourself be captivated by Egyptian art with its sarcophagi, sculptures and stunning Dendur Temple. Admire Greek ceramics, the splendor of Roman art, and the masterpieces of Velázquez, Dalí, Van Gogh, Monet, Botticelli, Vermeer, El Greco, Gauguin and many more. </p><p>Discover, among other works, the elegance of the Patio de Velez Blanco (Almeria) and the gate of Valladolid Cathedral.</p><p>With my guide, you will discover the highlights of the MET in a well structured and enriching tour, ensuring you make the most of every minute of your visit.</p><p>*** DUE TO TECHNICAL PROBLEMS, BOTH VIATOR AND TRIPADVISOR DO NOT SHOW THE LATEST REVIEWS. </p></div>",
