      "description": "<div><p>Looking for NYC's most famous and historic night spots? This 2-hour walking tour will introduce you to Greenwich Village and some of New York City's most famous bars, clubs, and theatres. See where careers have been made and great nights have been had. Stroll in the footsteps of Bob Dylan, Ray Charles, Chris Rock, Jimi Hendrix, Lenny Bruce, Idina Menzel and other figures who spent time in \"The Village.\" Get advice on which bar to visit and which theatres produce the most cutting edge material. Visit the hottest local eateries and learn the best time to get in line. This is the perfect mix of history and pop culture for anyone who is looking for a great nighttime activity in NYC. </p><p>Stops include Cafe Wha, The Comedy Cellar, The Stonewall Inn, The Public Theatre, The Blue Note and so many more! By the end of the evening you'll be an expert on the greatest night spots in Greenwich Village!</p></div>",
