      "name": "Boston and Harvard Small-Group Day Tour from New York City",
      "description": "<div><p>Make your way to the meeting point in Midtown Manhattan. Meet your group and settle in for the drive north.</p><p>Kick off your time in Boston at Copley Square. Your next stops are at Trinity Church, built in 1877, and the architectural gem that is Boston Public Library. After the Fairmont Copley Plaza and Commonwealth Avenue Mall, visit Harvard University’s main campus and see Harvard Yard, Old Yard, the John Harvard Statue, and Johnston Gate.</p><p>Then it’s on to the Freedom Trail, which brings Boston’s past to life. Stop at several sites along the trail, including the Massachusetts State House. The bustling Quincy Market is your final stop. There’s time to do some shopping before heading back to NYC where your tour ends back where you began.</p></div>",
