      "name": "Lower East Side Food and Culture Small-Group Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Discover the Lower East Side through its food and history on this 3-hour small-group tour.</p><p>Start with a sweet stroopwafel before tasting knishes at a classic Jewish bakery. Next, enjoy fresh mozzarella in Little Italy, once a vibrant hub of Italian immigrants.</p><p>Hear stories of the neighborhood's diverse past, including Poles, Jews, Italians, and the historic African burial ground. Then, head to Chinatown to sample pork buns and soup dumplings.</p><p>The tour wraps up back on the Lower East Side, leaving you free to explore more on your own. Wear weather-appropriate clothing and book 48 hours in advance. Come hungry, leave happy!</p></div>",
