      "name": "History of Alexander Hamilton in New York: An Audio Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>On this self-guided audio tour, you'll see New York City’s evolution through the eyes of one of its most famous and influential citizens, Alexander Hamilton, often called “the architect of the American financial system”. </p><p>Starting in front of the Charging Bull statue in New York’s oldest park, Bowling Green, you’ll walk nearly the entire perimeter of the original city to Trinity Church, where our tour ends. Along the way, you’ll trace Hamilton’s life from his arrival in New York at Battery Park, through his military service and his time in government, up until his death. As you make your way through the Financial District, you’ll come to understand the story of the American Revolution right where it took place, and Hamilton’s pivotal role.</p><p>Embark on this illuminating journey, where every step uncovers layers of history, commemorates the resilience of a nation, and honors the indelible mark left by Alexander Hamilton and the heroes of America’s past.</p></div>",
