      "name": "Brooklyn Pizza Walk to Discover New York's Best Slices",
      "description": "<div><p>Meet your guide at the morning or afternoon time you have chosen at Forcella in Brooklyn to begin your pizza-centric stroll in the Carroll Gardens neighborhood. This traditionally Italian-American area is thick with Italian cafes and shops along Court and Smith streets, and you stop to sample a slice in this unique corner of the city</p><p>Afterward, explore the trendy Cobble Hill neighborhood in Brooklyn, known for its vibrant cafes, bars, and restaurants lining Court Street, the main thoroughfare. There is a pizza pit stop in this hip district as well, along with an explanation of the area’s culinary history and traditional pizza-making techniques from your guide.</p><p>Your final tasting is in the Red Hook neighborhood in northwestern Brooklyn, where you can even pick up secret tips for making your own New York City pizza at home from a professional “pizzaiolo”, or pizza chef, while sampling a piping hot slice.</p><p>End your pizza adventure at Milk Bar in the Williamsburg neighborhood of Brooklyn, an easy walk to the L train to return to Manhattan.</p></div>",
