      "name": "Central Park Horse Carriage Ride (Short Loop)",
      "description": "<div><p>Welcome to Big Apples' short Central Park horse carriage tour! The tour starts at the corner of 59th street and 6th Avenue, following a short trip along the park on the 59th Street, the tour continues into the Central Park from 7th avenue with a nice view of the city. We stop at a point where the scenery is perfect to take pictures or just look around for a few minutes. Depending on where you look and what you see, the content of the tour changes. In NYC and central park, people around the US and the world gather in a festive atmosphere day and night, cold and warm! So, being on a horse carriage in Central Park where it is possible to have view of the city  in early evening and nights is like watching a panoramic view of the NYC, and its people who come from all around the world to meet at this city that \"never sleeps!\" This is a short, fun and relaxing experience. It is a \"must do\" in NYC!</p></div>",
