      "name": "The Best of the Metropolitan Museum of Art in 2 Hours",
      "description": "<div><p>Dive into two hours of art-fueled fun at the Met, one of the world’s largest and most diverse art museums. Join a small group—capped at just 15 guests—and head straight to the highlights (and oddities) of this sprawling collection that spans over 6,000 years and six continents.</p><p>Start by meeting your enthusiastic guide near the Met’s entrance, then meander through galleries packed with an eclectic mix of must-see masterpieces and lesser-known gems. Snap a photo of a strangely endearing limp hippo sculpture, do a double-take at an ancient Egyptian “wardrobe malfunction,” and uncover how a certain piece of Flemish dinnerware may not be as innocent as it first seems (family-friendly filters apply, of course).</p><p>In between giggles, explore some of the Met’s most iconic artworks, discovering fascinating stories behind figures like Monet and Van Gogh—whose personal lives were sometimes as colorful as their paintings. And yes, you might just find yourself on a quest for all things derrière, as you and your fellow art adventurers take part in a cheeky scavenger hunt that proves the Met holds a few unexpected surprises. This breezy, fast-paced tour ensures you’ll see the big-ticket items, dig into offbeat curiosities, and still have plenty of time to enjoy New York City afterward.</p></div>",
