      "name": "911 Ground Zero Tour & Museum Skip-the-Line Access",
      "description": "<div><p>Join a comprehensive, four-hour exploration of the World Trade Center site and uncover the extraordinary stories that emerged from September 11, 2001. Journey through the events of that day, following in the footsteps of first responders who descended “Stairwell B,” where firefighters defied the odds by surviving the collapse of a 110-story tower.</p><p>Hear about the “Angel of Stairwell B,” whose quick thinking saved an entire fire crew, and the astounding tale of the “9/11 Surfer,” who famously rode down 88 floors of crumbling debris. Learn how the new World Trade Center rose from the ashes and reflect on the memorial’s design and construction decisions as you stand among the tranquil pools at the Memorial Plaza.</p><p>Conclude with skip-the-ticket-line admission to the official September 11th Museum, where you’ll pass through security before embarking on a self-guided visit filled with artifacts, photographs, and oral histories that capture the tragedy and heroism of that day. This definitive Ground Zero experience goes beyond a simple tour—it’s a powerful tribute to resilience and a testament to human courage.</p></div>",
