      "name": "NYC TV & Movie Tour (On Location Tours)",
      "description": "<div><p>Enjoy a New York City TV and movie tour in classic Hollywood style—inside an actual film-used car, a 1957 Chevy 210 that once starred in <em>Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull</em>. Accommodating up to three passengers, this private tour immerses you in the city’s cinematic sights while you cruise the streets in a piece of movie history.</p><p>An actor-turned-guide will take you to locations featured in <em>Friends</em>, <em>Birdman</em>, <em>Girls</em>, <em>Glee</em>, and more, sharing insider tales about iconic scenes filmed throughout Manhattan. Expect stops such as the Daily Bugle office from <em>Spider-Man</em>, and the legendary Original Soupman that sparked a memorable <em>Seinfeld</em> character. Don’t forget to brush up on your favorite TV theme songs—this lively tour might just have you singing along. And, because it’s a private experience, you’ll typically finish an hour sooner than the standard group tours, letting you continue your NYC adventure right away.</p></div>",
