      "name": "New York City The Big Apple Helicopter Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Climb aboard a helicopter at the Manhattan heliport and lift off for a thrilling journey high above New York City. Glide south along the Hudson River, where you’ll spot One World Trade Center and the historic Woolworth Building towering over the Financial District. Hover over the Statue of Liberty for a one-of-a-kind perspective of this iconic monument, then swing by the Verrazano-Narrows Bridge, linking Staten Island and Brooklyn.</p><p>Loop back toward Midtown, taking in the New York Times Building, the Empire State Building, and the neon glow of Times Square. Catch a glimpse of the USS Intrepid museum ship along the way, then continue over the green expanse of Central Park. Farther uptown, gaze upon the enormity of St. John the Divine Cathedral and Columbia University, plus the storied Dakota apartments. Finally, pass by the George Washington Bridge before returning to the heliport.</p><p>Please note: The listed ticket price excludes the heliport fee, payable upon check-in.</p></div>",
