      "name": "Wall Street Insider Tour with a Finance Professional",
      "description": "<div><p>Meet your guide outside 15 Broad Street to start your deep dive into Wall Street’s past and present. Led by insiders who know these streets intimately, pass renowned financial landmarks like the New York Stock Exchange, Federal Reserve Bank of New York, Goldman Sachs, and Deutsche Bank (60 Wall Street). As you navigate Lower Manhattan’s narrow corridors, your guide shares firsthand tales that illuminate the area’s powerful influence.</p><p>Trace the Financial District’s journey over four centuries—from its Dutch origins to the modest roots of the NYSE, and eventually to the bustling hub of modern finance. Glimpse the spots where billion-dollar deals come together, learn about the immigrant entrepreneurs whose ambition shaped top U.S. banks, and appreciate the neighborhood’s rich architectural tapestry. Whether you call it the Financial District or FiDi, you’ll gain a fresh appreciation for the precinct that steers America’s economic fortunes.</p></div>",
