      "name": "Lunch & Dinner: Filet Mignon, Salad & Unlimited Fries",
      "description": "<div><p>Nestled in the heart of Midtown Manhattan, just steps from Carnegie Hall and Central Park, Brooklyn Diner 57th Street offers a warm welcome and a taste of New York’s rich food traditions. Since opening its doors, the Diner has become a beloved fixture in the city—celebrating the diverse, bold, and comforting flavors of Brooklyn in an upscale yet approachable diner setting.</p><p>Brooklyn Diner was built on the idea that comfort food can be elevated, nostalgic, and unforgettable. With its retro-inspired decor, vintage touches, and a menu full of diner classics with gourmet twists, it captures the essence of New York’s storied past and culinary present.</p><p>A favorite on the menu, the Steak, Salad &amp; Unlimited Fries features a perfectly cooked petite filet mignon, served with a crisp field green salad and unlimited golden French fries—hot, crispy, and endlessly satisfying. Whether you’re in for lunch, dinner, or a post-theater bite, it’s a timeless choice that embodies the diner’s signature style.</p></div>",
