      "name": "New York Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island Guided Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Your half-day adventure to two of New York’s most iconic landmarks starts early in Battery Park. After a security screening, hop aboard a ferry with your guide—round-trip tickets and entry included—ensuring you won’t miss this essential New York experience.</p><p>As you cruise the harbor, enjoy skyline views while hearing stories of the city’s past. First stop: Liberty Island, where you’ll come face to face with the Statue of Liberty and explore the museum dedicated to her history.</p><p>Next, re-board the ferry and sail on to Ellis Island. Learn about its pivotal role in American immigration, then enjoy some free time to immerse yourself in the Ellis Island Immigration Museum. Your tour concludes with the return trip to Battery Park.</p><p>Short on time? Consider the 2-hour option focused solely on Liberty Island.</p></div>",
