      "name": "New York Walking Tour with Private Local Guide",
      "description": "<div><p>Your guide meets you at your hotel in the morning to start your private, customizable tour of New York City. </p><p>Head to Times Square to see the neon lights of this top destination, and take a stroll through the Broadway Theater district, which consists of more than 40 theaters.</p><p>Continue to Rockefeller Center, a huge complex of 19 office buildings that also contains the Top of the Rock Observation Deck, The Rink, and Radio City Music Hall. Nearby, go inside the Beaux-Arts style building that houses the main branch of the New York Public Library, which contains a renowned collection of more than 53 million items. </p><p>View another impressive Beaux-Arts masterpiece at your next stop, Grand Central Terminal. Your guide shows you the intricacies of the bustling transit hub, including large sculptures and luminous paintings found on the ceiling during restoration work done in the 1990s. Enjoy some time for lunch (own expense).</p><p>Visit the 9/11 Memorial and Museum that now stands at the site of the destroyed World Trade Center. You can walk around the 9/11 Memorial Plaza to reflect on the events of September 11, 2001, or purchase tickets to enter the 9/11 Museum.</p><p>Your tour ends nearby at Wall Street where you pass be landmarks such as New York Stock Exchange, New York Board of Trade, and the bronze statue of the Charging Bull.</p></div>",
