      "name": "Toronto Harbour 1-Hour Sightseeing Cruise on Replica Steamship",
      "description": "<div><p>This sightseeing cruise departs from Toronto Harbour on the north shore of Lake Ontario. Climb aboard the elegant Oriole, a 76-foot, Great Lakes steamship replica. Choose from the spacious, open-air observation deck or settle into the air-conditioned cabin. Either way, the views will be up-close and incredible from the tranquil waters of Toronto’s naturally protected harbour.</p><p>Enjoy this entertaining and educational 60-minute sightseeing tour of Toronto, cruising past the city’s newly revitalized harbor-front and the Toronto Island parklands. Some of the sites include the iconic CN Tower and adjoining Rogers Centre, Queens Quay Terminal, Toronto Island Airport, Harbourfront Centre, HTO Park, Air Canada Centre, the Gibraltar Point Lighthouse, and more.</p><p>This multilingual audio tour offers informative narrations in seven languages (English, French, Spanish, Italian, German, Japanese, and Mandarin). Find out about the history of Toronto and all the aforementioned points of interest along the way.</p><p>A fully licensed cash bar provides a variety of beverages and snacks available for purchase on board. Restrooms are also available.</p></div>",
