      "shortDescription": "Get an overview of Chicago's history, architecture, and food in one awesome tour",
      "description": "Join a food tour through Chicago’s Loop district and the River North neighborhood with a local guide who knows where to find the city’s most popular eats. You'll try classic dishes like deep-dish pizza, Chicago-style hot dogs, and Italian beef while learning a bit about the city’s food history.\r\n\r\nStart with a Chicago-style hot dog, a local favorite with many opinions on how it should be made. Your guide will take you to try their go-to spot.\r\n\r\nNext, dig into deep-dish pizza at a well-known local pizzeria. This filling dish has been a part of Chicago’s food scene since the 1940s.\r\n\r\nAfter that, stop for an Italian beef sandwich at a longtime local restaurant known for doing it right.\r\n\r\nThe tour ends near a convenient ‘L’ train station. Your guide will also share dinner suggestions if you’re planning to keep exploring the city’s food scene later.",
