      "name": "Haunted Chicago Bus Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Get ready to embark on Chicago's most acclaimed paranormal experience! Now in its 24th year, the Original Chicago Hauntings Ghost Tour Bus takes you to the city's most actively haunted places, including the location of the tragic Eastland disaster, \"death alley\" where Iroquois Theater Fire happened, and the site of the most notorious gangland execution in history, The St. Valentine’s Day Massacre.You'll also discover where Chicago’s most famous ghost met her demise, “Resurrection Mary,”. Learn strange stories of the Hancock Building, one of the inspirations behind “Ghostbusters,” and the infamous Hull House, perhaps one of the inspirations for “Rosemary’s Baby”. Join this 3-hour, fully-narrated, luxury coach bus tour of Chicago's most haunted spots, and step off the bus to experience some of these spooky sites first-hand.</p></div>",
