      "name": "Chicago Small-Group Tour With Optional Architecture Cruise",
      "description": "<div><p>After pickup from a central meeting point, board your climate-controlled minibus.</p><p>Listen to historical and informational commentary from your guide as you admire the world's first skyscrapers in Downtown Chicago, known as \"The Loop.\" Take in panoramic views of Lake Michigan and other sights through the oversized windows on the minibus. </p><p>Drive through several Chicago neighborhoods like the Gold Coast and Lincoln Park to get a feel for daily life in the city. Make photo stops at Museum Campus, which boasts the best view of the Chicago skyline. Pass by other locations like the Willis Tower and Millennium Park. Please see the Itinerary section for a full list of attractions visited. </p><p>Optional Upgrade: For more sightseeing by water, upgrade your tour to include a boat ride down the Chicago River. This open-top boat tour provides an in-depth look at the architecture of Chicago. Additionally, learn about the role the river has played in the city’s history.</p></div>",
