      "name": "Routes POR Route 66 with Audio Guide",
      "description": "<div><p>Route 66, known as \"The Main Street of America\", runs through eight states from Chicago to Santa Monica. EN route to Illinois, POR Missouri, Kansas, Oklahoma, Texas, New Mexico, Arizona and California. Along DE way, it connects iconic cities such as St. Louis, Tulsa, Amarillo, Albuquerque, Flagstaff and Los Angeles, offering a unique experience through varied landscapes, from the Midwest Plains to the Southwest Deserts, each with its own history and culture.</p><p>Route Chicago : 50 points</p><p>Route DE Chicago to St. Louis : 56 points</p><p>Route San Luis : 13 points</p><p>Route DE San Luis to Joplin : 56 points</p><p>Route Joplin to Oklahoma city : 29 points</p><p>Route DE Oklahoma City to Amarillo : 27 points</p><p>Yellow Route to Santa Fe : 39 points</p><p>Route DE Santa Fe to Las Vegas : 80 points</p><p>Route DE Las Vegas to Los Angeles : 34 points</p><p>Total DE DE DE DE l’Or points of interest: 384</p></div>",
