      "description": "<div><p>The Art Institute of Chicago attracts nearly as many visitors as other leading galleries, like the Met, Louvre, and the British Museum - and with good reason! On this 2 - 2.5-hour, semi-private guided tour, you’ll be able to skip the line and explore the museum's most famous pieces with the help of an engaging guide.\r</p><p>Only the highest quality guide is equipped to introduce you to one of the greatest museums on earth. The Art Institute, one of the world’s great art museums, houses works that cover many centuries of art history, with works by Monet, Dalí, Warhol, Matisse, Van Gogh, Cézanne, Renoir, Hokusai, Wood, and more. Its known to have one of the world's greatest collections of Impressionist artworks (even rivaling the Musée D’Orsay in Paris). Your expert guide will help you explore the major artworks and hidden gems from this expansive collection and explain how this iconic American museum differs from its older European counterparts.</p></div>",
