      "name": "Private Old Montréal Walking Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Find out more about all the eras that shaped Montréal with this interesting 2-hour walking tour of Old Montréal, from the foundation of Fort Ville-Marie in 1642 to today’s modern city.  Visit important public squares, such as Place d'Armes, Place Royale, and Place Jacques-Cartier; pass by the Notre-Dame-de-Bon-Secours Chapel, City Hall, and walk along the former ''Wall Street'' of Canada; take a picture at the oldest building of the historic district, and enter Notre-Dame Basilica, if you choose ($). The historic heart of the city and its adjacent Old Port will help illuminate the story of one of the greatest cities in the Americas. Your guide will lead you through a maze of narrow streets where you can find a multitude of historic buildings. Explore the birthplace of our metropolis and experience a special voyage back in time! </p></div>",
