      "shortDescription": "Spend an exceptional day in the Lanaudière region from Montreal on a dogsled excursion near Rawdon!",
      "description": "<p>Spend an exceptional day in the Lanaudi&egrave;re region from Montreal on a dogsled excursion near Rawdon!</p>\n<p>A team of Alaskan dogs awaits you in Saint-Liguori to take you on a dog sledding excursion in the Lanaudi&egrave;re region, a winter experience not to be missed if you happen to be in Montreal! A driver-guide will pick you up in a minibus in Montreal to take you on an extraordinary day out in the heart of the snowy Lanaudi&egrave;re countryside, taking you first to the Montcalm ski resort for a morning's&nbsp;hike in the snow, then to Saint-Liguori for a dogsled ride near Rawdon.</p>\n<p>Whether you are the driver of the sled or a passenger, you will spend 1.5 to 2 hours on an unforgettable excursion pulled by your team of Alaskan huskies. An instructor from the Aventures Liguoriennes base will introduce you to dogsled driving (you can change places with your passenger to take turns driving) and guide you on a superb dogsled ride in the Lanaudi&egrave;re region. At the end of your escapade, you will enjoy a cuddle with the dogs, as well as a hot drink and a snack to round off the experience in style!</p>\n<p>If you would like to go dog sledding from Montreal, this day trip, including transport by minibus, is the ideal option!</p>",
