      "description": "<div><p>Discover Montreal's majestic beauty with the wind in your hair, as you set sail on a fascinating guided cruise on the St. Lawrence River. You'll pass by many of Montreal's iconic landmarks, including the Jacques Cartier Bridge, Habitat 67, and the Old Port. \r</p><p>Along the way, you might also spot some of the local wildlife, such as seals and various bird species. Keep your eyes peeled and your cameras primed.\r</p><p>Feeling hungry? Let yourself be tempted by the bistro menu, available on board at all times.\r</p><p>Sail from the Old Port of Montreal to the Boucherville Islands and enjoy a breathtaking view of downtown. Learn more about Quebec's metropolis with a guide, or simply relax on the outdoor terraces. A great way for first-time visitors to the city to see the sights.</p></div>",
