      "name": "Vancouver: The Grand Bike Tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Do it like the locals in Vancouver and get around by bicycle. This fact-packed 5-hour cycling tour is designed to show you the best bits of Downtown Vancouver and get you excited about discovering more of the city! \r</p><p>Starting with a tour of world-famous Stanley Park, hit the riding trails through old-growth forest and cycle along the spectacular seawall. After riding through English Bay, passing some of the hottest beaches in the city, we'll make our way to Granville Island. This cultural hot spot is famous for its arts scene, as well as great food and shopping. Poutine, anyone?\r</p><p>Next, follow the seawall along the south side of False Creek, taking in beautiful views of Vancouver’s modern architecture framed by the North Shore Mountains.\r</p><p>Finally, check out Vancouver’s vibrant Chinatown, and learn about the wild-frontier times as a logging outpost on the charming cobblestone streets of historic Gastown. What an adventure!</p></div>",
