      "name": "Grouse Mountain and Capilano Suspension Bridge Park tour",
      "description": "<div><p>Immerse yourself in the natural wonders surrounding Vancouver and the Burrard Inlet, with a visit to Capilano Suspension Bridge, the Capilano Salmon Hatchery and Grouse Mountain on this sightseeing tour.You'll kick your day off in Stanley Park, an urban oasis in the heart of the city then across the historic Lions Gate bridge to Vancouver's North Shore, before heading to the Capilano Suspension Bridge. Here, you'll stand above the towering cedar forest and watch the Capilano river wind through the trees below. Prepare to discover the stunning views, check out the First Nations artwork and get an adrenaline rush at the Cliff Walk.You can take in the beauty and the views of the Treetops Adventure Walk and then, continue on to the Capilano River Hatchery which is a project dedicated to several species of salmon and trout. You'll learn about the life cycle of salmon and even have the chance to view hatching and juvenile fish before they are released into a nearby river.Then, it's time to head to Grouse Mountain which offers ever-changing views as the Skyride ascends to the peak. Explore the Wildlife Refuge, admire the fantastic chainsaw carvings and learn about the local wildlife at the theater in the sky. This is your chance to be amazed and enchanted by the forests and mountains surrounding Vancouver!</p></div>",
