      "name": "Vancouver: Grouse Mountain Admission with Skyride Aerial Tram",
      "description": "<div><p>Escape from Vancouver for a few hours with a visit to Grouse Mountain — a year-round theme park celebrating the outdoor and cultural heritage of British Columbia. Get up close and personal with some of the region's incredible wildlife and enjoy fun shows, rides and exhibits, all set among the beautiful forests near Vancouver.</p><p>Start your visit by making your own way to Grouse Mountain, located just 8 miles (13km) from Vancouver at your leisure. The park is open from 9am to 9pm daily. Upon arrival at the park make your way up on the Skyride, spending as much time as you like enjoying the diverse activities and shows on offer. You can also add in additional park activities including mountain ropes and ziplining at your own expense.</p><p>Your purchase of the \"Peak Experience\" ticket offers access to a variety of Grouse Mountain amenities. Check out the 45-minute Lumberjack Show, performed in a 1900s-style logging camp. Or head to the Birds in Motion show, where you can observe these graceful aviary hunters as they soar through the air. Meanwhile over at the Wildlife Refuge, a ranger gives talks about the region's indigenous species including bears and other alpine creatures. During summer you can also take a trip on the Peak Chairlift, a summer attraction offering bird's-eye views of the mountain via an on-site ski lift.</p><p>During the winter you'll also enjoying ice skating at the park's outdoor rink, sleigh rides and trails for snowshoeing. A December \"Peak of Christmas\" celebration helps add to the holiday spirit.</p><p>Whatever time of year you visit, you admission also includes nature movies at the Theatre in the Sky, Peak Chalet access and round-trips on the Skyride, a 1-mile (1.6km) aerial tram offering sublime views of the surrounding area.</p></div>",
